{"type":"text","timestamp":1778894763350,"sessionID":"ses_1d19e0209ffejFC5EiVpSzatm6","part":{"id":"prt_e2e63f4db001n6xs2jE1sy4Z83","messageID":"msg_e2e6212380017jUgTofZsHoZOu","sessionID":"ses_1d19e0209ffejFC5EiVpSzatm6","type":"text","text":"I found a narrower follow-on to the successful branch-path cleanup: `ex_stage.sv` still recomputes the JAL target even though `id_stage.sv` already latched it. I’m writing the hypothesis around reusing that latched target and leaving only the JALR add in EX.","time":{"start":1778894763227,"end":1778894763348},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_03aa5841888522a1016a07c7ab155c819993a7f292efec3273","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778894764219,"sessionID":"ses_1d19e0209ffejFC5EiVpSzatm6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_XRj9VF7ungOLlKuWjZawJdgQ","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r3s0\n+title: \"Reuse latched JAL targets\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The core already latches `pc + imm` in ID for branch targets, but EX still\n+  recomputes the same add for JALs before redirecting fetch. Removing that\n+  duplicate 32-bit adder should trim a little more logic from the hot\n+  control-flow path without changing retirement, traps, or RVFI behavior.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Reuse the already-latched `branch_target` for JAL redirection in `ex_stage.sv`\n+  instead of recomputing `pc + imm` in EX. Keep the JALR path unchanged, since\n+  it still depends on forwarded `rs1`, but eliminate the redundant add on the\n+  common JAL path to reduce EX-stage combinational depth.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Use the latched branch target for JALs and keep only the JALR sum in EX.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r3s0\n+title: \"Reuse latched JAL targets\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The core already latches `pc + imm` in ID for branch targets, but EX still\n+  recomputes the same add for JALs before redirecting fetch. Removing that\n+  duplicate 32-bit adder should trim a little more logic from the hot\n+  control-flow path without changing retirement, traps, or RVFI behavior.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Reuse the already-latched `branch_target` for JAL redirection in `ex_stage.sv`\n+  instead of recomputing `pc + imm` in EX. Keep the JALR path unchanged, since\n+  it still depends on forwarded `rs1`, but eliminate the redundant add on the\n+  common JAL path to reduce EX-stage combinational depth.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Use the latched branch target for JALs and keep only the JALR sum in EX.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r3s0\n+title: \"Reuse latched JAL targets\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The core already latches `pc + imm` in ID for branch targets, but EX still\n+  recomputes the same add for JALs before redirecting fetch. Removing that\n+  duplicate 32-bit adder should trim a little more logic from the hot\n+  control-flow path without changing retirement, traps, or RVFI behavior.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Reuse the already-latched `branch_target` for JAL redirection in `ex_stage.sv`\n+  instead of recomputing `pc + imm` in EX. Keep the JALR path unchanged, since\n+  it still depends on forwarded `rs1`, but eliminate the redundant add on the\n+  common JAL path to reduce EX-stage combinational depth.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Use the latched branch target for JALs and keep only the JALR sum in EX.\"\n","additions":19,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml","time":{"start":1778894764185,"end":1778894764217}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_03aa5841888522a1016a07c7ab3c6881998aae8b374ba87ff5"}},"id":"prt_e2e63f555001WuVLkjBW9RDgih","sessionID":"ses_1d19e0209ffejFC5EiVpSzatm6","messageID":"msg_e2e6212380017jUgTofZsHoZOu"}}
