{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778899772317,"sessionID":"ses_1d1512f86ffe3q4D7LkG4NDDIj","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_A93op8wMHFduUWOICk9fIzNy","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r4s0\n+title: \"Latch writeback data in MEM\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  WB still rebuilds the final rd_wdata with a small mem_to_reg mux, and that\n+  signal fans out to both the regfile write port and the EX forwarding path.\n+  Hoisting the selection into MEM should shorten the common retire fanout\n+  without changing architectural results.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a latched rd_wdata field to the MEM/WB bundle, compute it in\n+  mem_stage.sv, and have wb_stage.sv forward that preselected value directly\n+  to the regfile and bypass network. This keeps the ISA and RVFI behavior\n+  unchanged while removing one more mux from the hot writeback path.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Extend the MEM/WB bundle with a latched rd_wdata field so writeback no longer has to remux ALU versus load data.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute the final writeback value alongside the existing load-data path and store it in the MEM/WB register.\"\n+  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Replace the final mem_to_reg mux with a direct pass-through of the preselected writeback value.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-ru