{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778887238400,"sessionID":"ses_1d210d03dffe8oVPbB9y0n0aS6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_wOU355Q3C5i32mDtCmqUy76h","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r1s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r1s1\n+title: \"Precompute branch targets in ID\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The current EX stage computes both the branch condition and the 32-bit\n+  PC+imm target in the same cycle. Moving the target add upstream should\n+  shorten the EX critical path and is a low-risk structural change for a\n+  branch-heavy CoreMark workload.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a `branch_target` field to the ID/EX bundle, compute B-type targets\n+  in `id_stage.sv`, and have `ex_stage.sv` reuse that precomputed target\n+  instead of redoing `pc + imm` in EX. This preserves the retirement and\n+  trap contract while trimming one adder from the execute-side timing path.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Extend the ID/EX bundle with a latched branch-target field.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Precompute branch targets during decode and store them in the pipeline register.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consume the latched branch target and remove the EX-side branch-target adder.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r1s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r1s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r1s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/