{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778894681536,"sessionID":"ses_1d19e0286ffe5oIsxEMgu6V0XU","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_gjjYUsmSjRTeinlEqi9RUbXR","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r3s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r3s1\n+title: \"Reuse ID target for JAL\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  EX still rebuilds the PC-relative jump target for JAL even though the\n+  same PC+imm value is already available from ID. Reusing that latched\n+  target should trim another 32-bit adder from the execute-side timing\n+  path without changing retirement, trap, or RVFI behavior.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Use the precomputed ID-stage branch target for JAL redirects and\n+  misalignment checks, and leave EX to compute only the rs1+imm target\n+  needed for JALR. This keeps control flow identical while removing one\n+  more hot add/mux pair from the EX critical path.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Reuse the latched PC-relative target for JAL so EX only computes the JALR target and associated trap/redirect bookkeeping.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r3s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r3s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r3s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r3s1.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r3s1\n+title: \"Reuse ID target for JAL\"\n+categor