{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778899797159,"sessionID":"ses_1d1513064ffe2IfR4mCxzSehIe","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_Rne2zJWB0YXrRC0Y8R6X0Fw0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r4s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r4s1\n+title: \"Hoist JALR target add\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  After hoisting branch targets and `pc+4` out of EX, the remaining hot\n+  control-flow arithmetic in the execute cone is the JALR `rs1 + imm`\n+  add. CoreMark still spends enough time on call/return paths that\n+  trimming that last adder should help Fmax without changing retirement.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a latched `jalr_target` field to the ID/EX bundle and compute the\n+  JALR destination in `id_stage.sv` from the decoded immediate plus a\n+  forwarded rs1 value, then have `ex_stage.sv` use the precomputed target\n+  for redirect and misalignment checks. This keeps EX as the architectural\n+  resolve point but removes the remaining JALR add/mux from its timing path.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add a latched `jalr_target` field to the ID/EX bundle.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Expose the forwarding information needed for an ID-side JALR target precompute.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Precompute and latch the JALR target alongside the existing decode metadata.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consume the latched JALR target and remove the EX-side `rs1 + imm` adder.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the new JALR precompute path through the top-level pipeline.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r4s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/