{"type":"text","timestamp":1778887185676,"sessionID":"ses_1d210cfd8ffexrsWPM1YWdtADu","part":{"id":"prt_e2df054e10012ZeYdwBgGCSs12","messageID":"msg_e2df00a8e001rYihdglMxzJ7C7","sessionID":"ses_1d210cfd8ffexrsWPM1YWdtADu","type":"text","text":"I’ve settled on a tiny BTB plus 2-bit counter predictor aimed at CoreMark’s hot loops and returns; writing the hypothesis YAML now.","time":{"start":1778887185633,"end":1778887185675},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0ba06b62653c7d37016a07aa1178c08198916f4ca29ad56583","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778887186698,"sessionID":"ses_1d210cfd8ffexrsWPM1YWdtADu","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_Md9ZE48yP2oAUVCCx4w9bzdM","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r1s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r1s2\n+title: \"Tiny BTB loop predictor\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark spends a lot of time in short loops and repeated call/return\n+  paths, so this core is paying the full EX-stage branch penalty on the\n+  same control transfers over and over. A very small predictor should\n+  remove those bubbles with limited area cost and without changing the\n+  in-order retirement contract.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a compact direct-mapped branch target buffer with 2-bit saturating\n+  counters and use it to speculatively redirect fetch on hot taken\n+  branches and jump targets from IF. Keep EX-stage resolution as the\n+  architectural source of truth so mispredict recovery stays simple and\n+  the RVFI / trap behavior remains unchanged.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Thread speculative next-PC selection through fetch and fall back to the existing redirect path on mispredicts.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Instantiate and connect the predictor update path using EX-stage resolution signals.\"\n+  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n+    description: \"Add a small direct-mapped BTB with 2-bit counters and update logic for taken branches and jumps.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r1s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r1s2.yaml\n===================================================================\