{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778892283934,"sessionID":"ses_1d1c30f89ffep6lZOdnnvoKGwJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_WH8FnTWvnzoBlye4bYCocKBI","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r2s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r2s2\n+title: \"Static BTFNT predictor\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark spends a lot of time in short loops, so the current EX-resolved\n+  branch path still pays avoidable fetch bubbles on repeated taken branches.\n+  A predictor that redirects IF earlier, but keeps EX as the source of truth,\n+  can improve CoreMark/MHz without changing retirement or RVFI behavior.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Replace the failed stateful BTB idea with a fully combinational static\n+  predictor in IF: predict backward conditional branches taken, forward\n+  conditional branches not taken, and always predict JALs taken from the\n+  fetched instruction. This keeps the predictor update path trivial, avoids\n+  speculative training state, and should hide more of the branch penalty on\n+  CoreMark's hot loops while preserving the existing mispredict redirect.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Use a static predictor to choose the speculative next PC before EX resolution.\"\n+  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n+    description: \"Add a small combinational BTFNT predictor that decodes the fetched instruction and emits the predicted next PC.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r2s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r2s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournamen