t_pc` breaks branch correctness on taken paths because the redirect target no longer has priority.\n- 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r3s2 (regression, -30.72%): A tiny call/return predictor only pays off if it resolves often enough to erase the fetch bubble; threading `pred_next_pc` and return-stack updates through retirement/recovery just adds control logic when the benchmark's control flow is still dominated by the simple EX redirect path.","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/LESSONS.md","time":{"start":1778899680918,"end":1778899680931}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0eeb2e8dd08afd9d016a07dae0c6ec819b9ffcba6bec98c625"}},"id":"prt_e2eaefe86001EK7y2fRQ11L1Bq","sessionID":"ses_1d1512fc8ffecO48H7Oi2Ag2CT","messageID":"msg_e2eaef064001i479SOI01n5Nj0"}}
