target adder.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the ID/EX bundle with a latched branch-target field.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Precompute branch targets during decode and store them in the pipeline register.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the latched branch target and remove the EX-side branch-target adder.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 296.38, \"delta_pct\": 4.79, \"vs_baseline\": 4.79, \"fmax_mhz\": 133.12, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterat...\n  Line 4: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny BTB loop predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time in short loops and repeated call/return\\npaths, so this core is paying the full EX-stage branch penalty on the\\nsame control transfers over and over. A very small predictor should\\nremove those bubbles with limited area cost and without changing the\\nin-order retirement contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time in short loops and repeated call/return\\npaths, so this core is paying the full EX-stage branch penalty on the\\nsame control transfers over and over. A very small predictor should\\nremove those bubbles with limited area cost and without changing the\\nin-order retirement contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a compact direct-mapped branch target buffer with 2-bit saturating\\ncounters and use it to speculatively redirect fetch on hot taken\\nbranches and jump targets from IF. Keep EX-stage resolution as the\\narchitectural source of truth so mispredict recovery stays simple and\\nthe RVFI / trap behavior remains unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread speculative next-PC selection through fetch and fall back to the existing redirect path on mispredicts.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate and connect the predictor update path using EX-stage resolution signals.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small direct-mapped BTB with 2-bit counters and update logic for taken branches and jumps.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread speculative next-PC selection through fetch and fall back to the existing redirect path on mispredicts.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate and connect the predictor update path using EX-stage resolution signals.\"}, {\"fi...\n  Line 5: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Resolve branches in ID\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"Branch-heavy CoreMark spends a lot of time paying the taken-branch\\nbubble created by waiting until EX to know the outcome. Moving the\\ncommon conditional-branch decision into ID should cut one wrong-path\\ncycle while also shortening the EX timing cone.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Branch-heavy CoreMark spends a lot of time paying the taken-branch\\nbubble created by waiting until EX to know the outcome. Moving the\\ncommon conditional-branch decision into ID should cut one wrong-path\\ncycle while also shortening the EX timing cone.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add local operand forwarding into ID so BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU can\\nbe resolved as soon as decode has the operands, using the branch target\\nalready precomputed in ID. Keep EX as the architectural fallback for\\nthe remaining jump/misalign cases, but stop burning a full EX-stage\\nbubble on ordinary taken branches.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the pipeline bundle with any extra ID-side branch resolve state needed for early branch handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add branch compare logic and local forwarding so common conditional branches can resolve in decode.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Teach the hazard logic when an ID-resolved branch still needs a stall versus when it can redirect immediately.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the new ID-stage branch decision into fetch/redirect control without changing the RVFI contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the pipeline bundle with any extra ID-side branch resolve state needed for early branch handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add branch compare logic and local forwarding...\n  Line 6: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r2s1\", \"title\": \"Latch pc+4 in ID\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The execute stage still rebuilds the sequential fall-through PC in the hot\\nretirement path, even though that value is known as soon as the IF/ID PC is\\nlatched. Hoisting that adder out of EX should trim a little more logic from\\nthe branch/link critical path without changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The execute stage still rebuilds the sequential fall-through PC in the hot\\nretirement path, even though that value is known as soon as the IF/ID PC is\\nlatched. Hoisting that adder out of EX should trim a little more logic from\\nthe branch/link critical path without changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a latched `pc_plus4` field to the ID/EX bundle, compute it in\\n`id_stage.sv`, and have `ex_stage.sv` reuse that precomputed value for JAL\\nlink writeback and fall-through `pc_next` selection. This is a structural\\ntiming cleanup: it removes another 32-bit add from EX while preserving the\\nexisting control, RVFI, and trap contract.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the ID/EX bundle with a latched pc_plus4 field.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and store pc_plus4 alongside the decoded instruction metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Reuse the latched pc_plus4 for JAL writeback and sequential next-PC selection.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the ID/EX bundle with a latched pc_plus4 field.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and store pc_plus4 alongside the decoded instruction metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Reuse the latched pc_plus4 for JAL writeback and sequential next-PC selection.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 311.83, ...\n  Line 7: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r2s2\", \"title\": \"Static BTFNT predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time in short loops, so the current EX-resolved\\nbranch path still pays avoidable fetch bubbles on repeated taken branches.\\nA predictor that redirects IF earlier, but keeps EX as the source of truth,\\ncan improve CoreMark/MHz without changing retirement or RVFI behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time in short loops, so the current EX-resolved\\nbranch path still pays avoidable fetch bubbles on repeated taken branches.\\nA predictor that redirects IF earlier, but keeps EX as the source of truth,\\ncan improve CoreMark/MHz without changing retirement or RVFI behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the failed stateful BTB idea with a fully combinational static\\npredictor in IF: predict backward conditional branches taken, forward\\nconditional branch