{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778899701691,"sessionID":"ses_1d1512fc8ffecO48H7Oi2Ag2CT","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_ZIVLd3iRw9V7UjaqXiNkXKoy","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl","offset":1,"limit":20},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\"id\": \"baseline-bench-2a72da6\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 282.82, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 127.03, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9563, \"ff\": 1866, \"seeds\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-15T23:18:18.323525Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\n2: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Zero-wait load bypass\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark is load-heavy, and the current 5-stage pipe pays a full bubble\\non every load-use pair even when the data memory is zero-wait. Removing\\nthat unnecessary interlock should raise iterations per cycle without\\nchanging the ISA or the top-level RVFI contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark is load-heavy, and the current 5-stage pipe pays a full bubble\\non every load-use pair even when the data memory is zero-wait. Removing\\nthat unnecessary interlock should raise iterations per cycle without\\nchanging the ISA or the top-level RVFI contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a combinational MEM-to-EX bypass for load results so a dependent\\ninstruction can consume the loaded word in the next cycle instead of\\nstalling behind the load. Keep the existing dmem backpressure stall\\npath intact, but stop treating zero-wait load-use pairs as mandatory\\nbubbles.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the combinational load result and metadata needed for a same-cycle bypass.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a forwarding input that can source operands directly from the current MEM-stage load data.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Relax the load-use interlock when the zero-wait MEM bypass can satisfy the dependency.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the new MEM-stage bypass signals through the pipeline.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the combinational load result and metadata needed for a same-cycle bypass.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a forwarding input that can source operands directly from the current MEM-stage load data.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Relax the load-use inter... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n3: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Precompute branch targets in ID\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current EX stage computes both the branch condition and the 32-bit\\nPC+imm target in the same cycle. Moving the target add upstream should\\nshorten the EX critical path and is a low-risk structural change for a\\nbranch-heavy CoreMark workload.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current EX stage computes both the branch condition and the 32-bit\\nPC+imm target in the same cycle. Moving the target add upstream should\\nshorten the EX critical path and is a low-risk structural change for a\\nbranch-heavy CoreMark workload.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a `branch_target` field to the ID/EX bundle, compute B-type targets\\nin `id_stage.sv`, and have `ex_stage.sv` reuse that precomputed target\\ninstead of redoing `pc + imm` in EX. This preserves the retirement and\\ntrap contract while trimming one adder from the execute-side timing path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the ID/EX bundle with a latched branch-target field.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Precompute branch targets during decode and store them in the pipeline register.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the latched branch target and remove the EX-side branch-target adder.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the ID/EX bundle with a latched branch-target field.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Precompute branch targets during decode and store them in the pipeline register.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the latched branch target and remove the EX-side branch-target adder.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 296.38, \"delta_pct\": 4.79, \"vs_baseline\": 4.79, \"fmax_mhz\": 133.12, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterat... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n4: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny BTB loop predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time in short loops and repeated call/return\\npaths, so this core is paying the full EX-stage branch penalty on the\\nsame control transfers over and over. A very small predictor should\\nremove those bubbles with limited area cost and without changing the\\nin-order retirement contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time in short loops and repeated call/return\\npaths, so this core is paying the full EX-stage branch penalty on the\\nsame control transfers over and over. A very small predictor should\\nremove those bubbles with limited area cost and without changing the\\nin-order retirement contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a compact direct-mapped branch target buffer with 2-bit saturating\\ncounters and use it to speculatively redirect fetch on hot taken\\nbranches and jump targets from IF. Keep EX-stage resolution as the\\narchitectural source of truth so mispredict recovery stays simple and\\nthe RVFI / trap behavior remains unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread speculative next-PC selection through fetch and fall back to the existing redirect path on mispredicts.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate and connect the predictor update path using EX-stage resolution signals.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small direct-mapped BTB with 2-bit counters and update logic for taken branches and jumps.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread speculative next-PC selection through fetch and fall back to the existing redirect path on mispredicts.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate and connect the predictor update path using EX-stage resolution signals.\"}, {\"fi... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n5: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Resolve branches in ID\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"Branch-heavy CoreMark spends a lot of time paying the taken-branch\\nbubble created by waiting until EX to know the outcome. Moving the\\ncommon conditional-branch decision into ID should cut one wrong-path\\ncycle while also shortening the EX timing cone.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Branch-heavy CoreMark spends a lot of time paying the taken-branch\\nbubble created by waiting until EX to know the outcome. Moving the\\ncommon conditional-branch decision into ID should cut one wrong-path\\ncycle while also shortening the EX timing cone.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add local operand forwarding into ID so BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU can\\nbe resolved as soon as decode has the operands, using the branch target\\nalready precomputed in ID. Keep EX as the architectural fallback for\\nthe remaining jump/misalign cases, but stop burning a full EX-stage\\nbubble on ordinary taken branches.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the pipeline bundle with any extra ID-side branch resolve state needed for early branch handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add branch compare logic and local forwarding so common conditional branches can resolve in decode.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Teach the hazard logic when an ID-resolved branch still needs a stall versus when it can redirect immediately.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the new ID-stage branch decision into fetch/redirect control without changing the RVFI contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the pipeline bundle with any extra ID-side branch resolve state needed for early branch handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add branch compare logic and local forwarding... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n6: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r2s1\", \"title\": \"Latch pc+4 in ID\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The execute stage still rebuilds the sequential fall-through PC in the hot\\nretirement path, even though that value is known as soon as the IF/ID PC is\\nlatched. Hoisting that adder out of EX should trim a little more logic from\\nthe branch/link critical path without changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The execute stage still rebuilds the sequential fall-through PC in the hot\\nretirement path, even though that value is known as soon as the IF/ID PC is\\nlatched. Hoisting that adder out of EX should trim a little more logic from\\nthe branch/link critical path without changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a latched `pc_plus4` field to the ID/EX bundle, compute it in\\n`id_stage.sv`, and have `ex_stage.sv` reuse that precomputed value for JAL\\nlink writeback and fall-through `pc_next` selection. This is a structural\\ntiming cleanup: it removes another 32-bit add from EX while preserving the\\nexisting control, RVFI, and trap contract.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the ID/EX bundle with a latched pc_plus4 field.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and store pc_plus4 alongside the decoded instruction metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Reuse the latched pc_plus4 for JAL writeback and sequential next-PC selection.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the ID/EX bundle with a latched pc_plus4 field.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and store pc_plus4 alongside the decoded instruction metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Reuse the latched pc_plus4 for JAL writeback and sequential next-PC selection.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 311.83, ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n7: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r2s2\", \"title\": \"Static BTFNT predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time in short loops, so the current EX-resolved\\nbranch path still pays avoidable fetch bubbles on repeated taken branches.\\nA predictor that redirects IF earlier, but keeps EX as the source of truth,\\ncan improve CoreMark/MHz without changing retirement or RVFI behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time in short loops, so the current EX-resolved\\nbranch path still pays avoidable fetch bubbles on repeated taken branches.\\nA predictor that redirects IF earlier, but keeps EX as the source of truth,\\ncan improve CoreMark/MHz without changing retirement or RVFI behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the failed stateful BTB idea with a fully combinational static\\npredictor in IF: predict backward conditional branches taken, forward\\nconditional branches not taken, and always predict JALs taken from the\\nfetched instruction. This keeps the predictor update path trivial, avoids\\nspeculative training state, and should hide more of the branch penalty on\\nCoreMark's hot loops while preserving the existing mispredict redirect.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use a static predictor to choose the speculative next PC before EX resolution.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small combinational BTFNT predictor that decodes the fetched instruction and emits the predicted next PC.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use a static predictor to choose the speculative next PC before EX resolution.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small combinational BTFNT predictor that decodes the fetched instruction and emits the predicted next PC.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n8: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r3s0\", \"