{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778899717204,"sessionID":"ses_1d1512fc8ffecO48H7Oi2Ag2CT","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_ShTlL48gQdluOb8d14JR3om8","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r4s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r4s2\n+title: \"Advisory BTFNT fetch hint\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark still spends a lot of time in tight loops and repeated control\n+  transfers, so the core keeps paying the EX-stage branch bubble on paths\n+  that are easy to predict statically. A predictor with no training state\n+  should be cheap enough for this tiny FPGA core.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Fold a purely combinational BTFNT hint into IF: predict backward\n+  conditional branches taken, forward conditional branches not taken, and\n+  direct JALs taken. Keep EX redirect as the architectural source of truth\n+  so mispredict recovery stays simple and RVFI/trap behavior is unchanged,\n+  but hide more fetch bubbles on CoreMark's hot loops.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add a stateless static branch-direction predictor that chooses the speculative next PC while still yielding to EX-stage redirects.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r4s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r4s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r4s2.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r4s2.yam