{"type":"text","timestamp":1778929974089,"sessionID":"ses_1cf8402bdffejHwQXRomOTdHi7","part":{"id":"prt_e307d3b2c0013XmijJSDKKOgJw","messageID":"msg_e307cd3bf001pUYKa7Vy80UMad","sessionID":"ses_1cf8402bdffejHwQXRomOTdHi7","type":"text","text":"I’ve narrowed it to a small control-path cleanup: exact source-operand masks, used only to stop the load-use interlock from comparing unused rs fields. That keeps the change local and avoids the wider bundle regressions from the last round.","time":{"start":1778929974060,"end":1778929974071},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0b8d9868d017a77d016a085135c9848199a2d5283ee82b4c04","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778929975112,"sessionID":"ses_1cf8402bdffejHwQXRomOTdHi7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_pDSbx1rQtAFIxvyOLr2brJ9H","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r10s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-001-r10s0\n+title: \"Decoder-aligned stall masks\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark spends a lot of time on instructions that do not read both\n+  source registers. The current load-use interlock still compares raw rs\n+  fields unconditionally, so it burns fanout and can inject false bubbles\n+  on common immediate and U-type instructions.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add exact `uses_rs1` / `uses_rs2` metadata to the fetch-time predecode\n+  bundle, derived from the same opcode-class rules the decoder uses, and\n+  use those bits to gate the load-use compare tree in `hazard_unit.sv`.\n+  This should remove avoidable stall checks on instructions that do not\n+  architecturally read rs2, while keeping RVFI, traps, and forwarding\n+  behavior unchanged.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` to the predecode bundle so source-read intent can ride with the fetched instruction.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute and latch exact source-operand-use bits alongside the existing predecode fields.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate the load-use compare logic with the source-read bits so unused rs fields cannot trigger false stalls.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r10s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r10s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r10s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r10s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@\n+id: hyp-20260516-001-r10s0\n+title: \"Decoder-aligned stall masks\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark spends a lot of time on instructions that do not read both\n+  source registers. The current load-use interlock still compares raw rs\n+  fields unconditionally, so it burns fanout and can inject false bubbles\n+  on common immediate and U-type instructions.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add exact `uses_rs1` / `uses_rs2` metadata to the fetch-time predecode\n+  bundle, derived from the same opcode-class rules the decoder uses, and\n+  use those bits to gate the load-use compare tree in `hazard_unit.sv`.\n+  This should remove avoidable stall checks on instructions that do not\n+  architecturally read rs2, while keeping RVFI, traps, and forwarding\n+  behavior unchanged.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` to the predecode bundle so source-read intent can ride with the fetched instruction.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute and latch exact source-operand-use bits alongside the existing predecode fields.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate the load-use compare logic with the source-read bits so unused rs fields cannot trigger false stalls.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r10s0.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r10s0.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tourname