{"type":"text","timestamp":1778933767728,"sessionID":"ses_1cf4ad3e2ffelQKRHQLBVGeaYa","part":{"id":"prt_e30b71b54001i3qnWp3h5qDSdO","messageID":"msg_e30b6fe7a001UAtO02OW1f5TWi","sessionID":"ses_1cf4ad3e2ffelQKRHQLBVGeaYa","type":"text","text":"Writing the hypothesis now. I’m keeping it to a single hot-path hoist: cache `pc+4` in IF, stop recomputing it in ID, and leave the rest of the control flow unchanged.","time":{"start":1778933766997,"end":1778933767723},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_040dd5069238a07a016a086006bcbc819b9c349b84d58de0d7","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778933775148,"sessionID":"ses_1cf4ad3e2ffelQKRHQLBVGeaYa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_wt2VxyHSjVJ3jT8WqRMpo96N","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r11s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-001-r11s0\n+title: \"Cache pc+4 in IF\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The sequential fall-through PC is needed on every instruction, but the\n+  current core still recomputes `pc + 4` in ID. Hoisting that universal add\n+  into fetch should trim a small amount of always-on decode-path logic and\n+  reduce fanout through the hot IF/ID -> ID/EX boundary.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a cached `pc_plus4` field to the IF/ID bundle, compute it once in\n+  `if_stage.sv`, and have `id_stage.sv` latch that value directly instead of\n+  rebuilding `pc + 4` every cycle. This keeps retirement, traps, and RVFI\n+  behavior unchanged while moving a universal 32-bit add out of the ID hot\n+  path.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add `pc_plus4` to the IF/ID bundle so fetch can carry the sequential PC forward.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute and latch `pc_plus4` alongside the fetched instruction metadata.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consume the cached sequential PC instead of recomputing `pc + 4` in decode.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r11s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r11s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-2026