{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778907819008,"sessionID":"ses_1d0d5cb85ffe5rZDnKL7QQils7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_s3haRER6pwzKlTCd1eeZfJXY","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r6s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-001-r6s0\n+title: \"Operand-use hazard gating\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The core already predecodes opcode and register slices, but the hazard\n+  and forwarding logic still compares raw rs fields for every instruction.\n+  That creates avoidable compare fanout and can also stall on rs2 bits that\n+  are really immediates in single-source instructions.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add predecoded operand-use flags so the pipe only compares rs1/rs2 when\n+  the current instruction actually reads them. Carry those flags through\n+  IF/ID and ID/EX, then gate load-use detection and EX forwarding selects\n+  with them to remove spurious stalls and trim hot compare logic without\n+  changing RVFI or retirement behavior.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Extend the pipeline bundles with operand-use bits for rs1/rs2 so downstream hazard and forwarding logic can ignore unused source fields.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Predecode which source operands are actually read and carry those bits alongside the fetched instruction.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch the operand-use flags into ID/EX so execute-side forwarding can skip irrelevant source compares.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use checks with the operand-use flags to avoid false stalls on immediate and single-source instructions.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Use the operand-use flags to prune unnecessary rs compare logic in the EX-stage forwarding network.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r6s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r6s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r6s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r6s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@\n+id: hyp-20260516-001-r6s0\n+title: \"Operand-use hazard gating\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The core already predecodes opcode and register slices, but the hazard\n+  and forwarding logic still compares raw rs fields for every instruction.\n+  That creates avoidable compare fanout and can also stall on rs2 bits that\n+  are really immediates in single-source instructions.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add predecoded operand-use flags so the pipe only compares rs1/rs2 when\n+  the current instruction actually reads them. Carry those flags through\n+  IF/ID and ID/EX, then gate load-use detection and EX forwarding selects\n+  with them to remove spurious stalls and trim hot compare logic without\n+  changing RVFI or retirement behavior.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Extend the pipeline bundles with operand-use bits for rs1/rs2 so downstream hazard and forwarding logic can ignore unused source fields.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Predecode which source operands are actually read and carry those bits alongside the fetched instruction.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch the operand-use flags into ID/EX so execute-side forwarding can skip irrelevant source compares.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use checks with the operand-use flags to avoid false stalls on immediate and single-source instructions.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Use the operand-use flags to prune unnecessary rs compare logic in the EX-stage forwarding network.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r6s0.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r6s0.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r6s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r6s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r6s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@\n+id: hyp-20260516-001-r6s0\n+title: \"Operand-use hazard gating\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The core already predecodes opcode and register slices, but the hazard\n+  and forwarding logic still compares raw rs fields for every instruction.\n+  That creates avoidable compare fanout and can also stall on rs2 bits that\n+  are really immediates in single-source instructions.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add predecoded operand-use flags so the pipe only compares rs1/rs2 when\n+  the current instruction actually reads them. Carry those flags through\n+  IF/ID and ID/EX, then gate load-use detection and EX forwarding selects\n+  with them to remove spurious stalls and trim hot compare logic without\n+  changing RVFI or retirement behavior.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Extend 