{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778919422863,"sessionID":"ses_1d0264394ffehpd2FSJobtZhHW","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_q9GDobsKRtXLv9DPkLRxyJUM","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r8s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-001-r8s0\n+title: \"Decoder-aligned operand-use gating\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark spends a lot of time on instructions that do not actually read both\n+  source registers. The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares raw\n+  rs fields unconditionally, which adds fanout on the hot control path and can\n+  also create avoidable load-use stalls on immediate-style ops.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add exact `uses_rs1`/`uses_rs2` bits to the predecode and control path using\n+  the same opcode/funct classification as the decoder, then gate load-use\n+  detection and EX forwarding compares with those bits. That should remove\n+  false stalls on single-source instructions and trim always-on compare logic\n+  without changing RVFI, traps, or in-order retirement.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add source-operand-use fields to the predecode/control bundles and keep the classification shape shared across stages.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute and latch the exact operand-use bits alongside the existing predecode metadata.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Populate the same operand-use classification from the validated opcode/funct table so IF and decode stay aligned.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Carry the operand-use bits into ID/EX so downstream logic can rely on the same source-operand semantics.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use detection with the operand-use bits to avoid false stalls on instructions that do not read rs2.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Use the operand-use bits to prune unnecessary rs compare logic in the forwarding network.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r8s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r8s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r8s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r8s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@\n+id: hyp-20260516-001-r8s0\n+title: \"Decoder-aligned operand-use gating\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark spends a lot of time on instructions that do not actually read both\n+  source registers. The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares raw\n+  rs fields unconditionally, which adds fanout on the hot control path and can\n+  also create avoidable load-use stalls on immediate-style ops.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add exact `uses_rs1`/`uses_rs2` bits to the predecode and control path using\n+  the same opcode/funct classification as the decoder, then gate load-use\n+  detection and EX forwarding compares with those bits. That should remove\n+  false stalls on single-source instructions and trim always-on compare logic\n+  without changing RVFI, traps, or in-order retirement.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add source-operand-use fields to the predecode/control bundles and keep the classification shape shared across stages.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute and latch the exact operand-use bits alongside the existing predecode metadata.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Populate the same operand-use classification from the validated opcode/funct table so IF and decode stay aligned.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Carry the operand-use bits into ID/EX so downstream logic can rely on the same source-operand semantics.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use detection with the operand-use bits to avoid false stalls on instructions that do not read rs2.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Use the operand-use bits to prune unnecessary rs compare logic in the forwarding network.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r8s0.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r8s0.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r8s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r8s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r8s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@\n+id: hyp-20260516-001-r8s0\n+title: \"Decoder-aligned operand-use gating\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark spends a lot of time on instructions that do not actually read both\n+  source registers. The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares raw\n+  rs fields unconditionally, which adds fanout on the hot control path and can\n+  also create avoidable load-use stalls on immediate-style ops.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add exact `uses_rs1`/`uses_rs2` bits to the predecode and control path using\n+  the same opcod