{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778925156915,"sessionID":"ses_1cfcdc55affeSmtuvF69A5uIwp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_PbZr2XrzpjnwSLlvdiJVTqQT","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r9s1.yaml","offset":1,"limit":120},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r9s1.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260516-002-r9s1\n2: title: \"One-hot decode classes\"\n3: category: structural\n4: motivation: |\n5:   The hot decode path still rebuilds opcode/funct legality and instruction\n6:   class information from the raw 32-bit instruction in ID. Hoisting that\n7:   classification into fetch-time predecode should cut repeated case-tree\n8:   work and narrow the control fanout seen by the rest of the pipe.\n9: hypothesis: |\n10:   Add compact one-hot instruction-class metadata to the IF-stage predecode\n11:   bundle, then have ID consume those cached classes when forming control and\n12:   hazard inputs instead of repeatedly re-decoding the same opcode/funct\n13:   patterns from `instr[31:0]`. Keep the decoder's legality rules unchanged,\n14:   but make the common control path structurally narrower so EX and MEM see\n15:   less combinational decode work on every cycle.\n16: expected_impact:\n17:   fitness_delta_pct: 4\n18:   confidence: medium\n19: changes:\n20:   - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n21:     description: \"Extend the predecode and pipeline bundles with compact one-hot instruction-class metadata.\"\n22:   - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n23:     description: \"Compute and latch the instruction-class metadata once at fetch time.\"\n24:   - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n25:     description: \"Consume the predecoded classes when building control signals instead of re-decoding from the full instruction word.\"\n26:   - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n27:     description: \"Keep legality semantics identical while simplifying dispatch around the predecoded instruction class inputs.\"\n\n(End of file - total 27 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260516-002-r9s1\ntitle: \"One-hot decode classes\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The hot decode path still rebuilds opcode/funct legality and instruction\n  class information from the raw 32-bit instruction in ID. Hoisting that\n  classification into fetch-time predecode should cut repeated case-tree\n  work and narrow the control fanout seen by the rest of the pipe.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add compact one-hot instruction-class metadata to the IF-stage predecode\n  bundle, then have ID consume those cached classes when forming control and\n  hazard inputs instead of repeatedly re-decoding the same opcode/funct\n  patterns from `instr[31:0]`. Keep the decoder's legality rules unchanged,\n  but make the common control path structurally narrower so EX and MEM see\n  less combinational decode work on every cycle.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r9s1.yaml","time":{"start":1778925156652,"end":1778925156913}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0ea1f5497bbf021a016a083e645dac81989a084b6828ac7641"}},"id":"prt_e3033b8ed0011u0z7k99FBFIQi","sessionID":"ses_1cfcdc55affeSmtuvF69A5uIwp","messageID":"msg_e3033a18a001pyb2Lnux9eobTC"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778925156927,"sessionID":"ses_1cfcdc55affeSmtuvF69A5uIwp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_sy2aJOA5u3sKCleOF6lHAxcm","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r9s2.yaml","offset":1,"limit":120},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r9s2.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260516-003-r9s2\n2: title: \"Tiny bimodal branch predictor\"\n3: category: predictor\n4: motivation: |\n5:   CoreMark still spends a meaningful fraction of its time on the same\n6:   conditional backedges and short control-flow loops. The earlier static\n7:   and stack-based predictor ideas were either too expensive or too broad,\n8:   so a smaller learned direction predictor is the best remaining angle.\n9: hypothesis: |\n10:   Add a tiny direct-mapped bimodal predictor that stores only 2-bit taken\n11:   confidence for conditional branches, with the existing IF-stage immediate\n12:   decode used to choose between fall-through and the predicted branch target.\n13:   Update the table only from retired conditional branches, keep EX-stage\n14:   resolution authoritative for recovery, and avoid BTB or return-stack\n15:   target storage entirely so the predictor stays cheap enough for this FPGA.\n16: expected_impact:\n17:   fitness_delta_pct: 5\n18:   confidence: medium\n19: changes:\n20:   - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n21:     description: \"Use a small bimodal direction predictor to speculatively choose fall-through vs the decoded branch target before EX resolves the branch.\"\n22:   - file: rtl/core.sv\n23:     description: \"Wire retired conditional-branch outcome information into the predictor update path without changing the RVFI or trap contract.\"\n24:   - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n25:     description: \"Add a tiny direct-mapped 2-bit branch-direction table with conservative fall-through defaults and retirement-time updates.\"\n\n(End of file - total 25 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260516-003-r9s2\ntitle: \"Tiny bimodal branch predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  CoreMark still spends a meaningful fraction of its time on the same\n  conditional backedges and short control-flow loops. The earlier static\n  and stack-based predictor ideas were either too expensive or too broad,\n  so a smaller learned direction predictor is the best remaining angle.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny direct-mapped bimodal predictor that stores only 2-bit taken\n  confidence for conditional branches, with the existing IF-stage immediate\n  decode used to choose between fall-through and the predicted branch target.\n  Update the table only from retired conditional branches, keep EX-stage\n  resolution authoritative for recovery, and avoid BTB or return-stack\n  target storage entirely so the predictor stays cheap enough for this FPGA.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r9s2.yaml","time":{"start":1778925156700,"end":1778925156921}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0ea1f5497bbf021a016a083e645db881989e8c69c66d7bfced"}},"id":"prt_e3033b94a001hIDwgoWkQWDyh0","sessionID":"ses_1cfcdc55affeSmtuvF69A5uIwp","messageID":"msg_e3033a18a001pyb2Lnux9eobTC"}}
