{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778925174102,"sessionID":"ses_1cfcdc55affeSmtuvF69A5uIwp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_w7xGFSp28miZpbU9b69QPHpT","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r9s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-001-r9s0\n+title: \"Source-read stall masks\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The load-use interlock still compares both source register fields for every\n+  instruction, even when the opcode class does not architecturally read one\n+  or both sources. That creates avoidable compare fanout and can inject false\n+  bubbles on common immediate and U-type instructions in CoreMark.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add exact `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` bits to the IF-stage predecode bundle,\n+  then gate `hazard_unit.sv`'s load-use compare logic with those bits so it\n+  only checks source registers that the current instruction actually reads.\n+  This should remove false stalls on OP-IMM, LOAD, JALR, LUI, AUIPC, JAL,\n+  FENCE, and SYSTEM forms while slightly shrinking the hot hazard path, all\n+  without changing RVFI, traps, or retirement order.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add source-read flags to the predecode bundle so later stages can distinguish architecturally used vs unused rs fields.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute and latch exact `uses_rs1` / `uses_rs2` bits alongside the existing predecode metadata.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate the load-use compare tree with the source-read flags so unused rs fields cannot trigger false stalls.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r9s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/exp