{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778933716541,"sessionID":"ses_1cf4ad4ceffec3VftqnhrCFev2","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_vvMJONJ0s5drbzF64BWmU6mu","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r11s2.yaml","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r11s2.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260516-003-r11s2\n2: title: \"Retired loop-backedge predictor\"\n3: category: predictor\n4: motivation: |\n5:   CoreMark still burns cycles on the same hot loop backedges, but the\n6:   broader predictor attempts paid too much in IF logic or speculative\n7:   state. A tiny predictor anchored to retired control-flow state is the\n8:   narrowest remaining way to hide those fetch bubbles without changing\n9:   the architectural redirect contract.\n10: hypothesis: |\n11:   Add a single-entry loop-backedge predictor that remembers the most\n12:   recent retired taken conditional branch PC and target, then speculates\n13:   only on exact PC hits for backward branches. Train it strictly from\n14:   retired branch outcomes, keep EX-stage redirect authoritative for every\n15:   recovery path, and avoid any extra speculative training state so the\n16:   predictor stays small enough to help CoreMark without dragging Fmax.\n17: expected_impact:\n18:   fitness_delta_pct: 4\n19:   confidence: medium\n20: changes:\n21:   - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n22:     description: \"Consume a tiny loop-backedge hint for speculative next-PC selection, but always yield to EX-stage redirect recovery.\"\n23:   - file: rtl/core.sv\n24:     description: \"Wire retired conditional-branch outcome information into the predictor update path without changing RVFI or trap behavior.\"\n25:   - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n26:     description: \"Add a single-entry loop-backedge predictor with exact-PC tagging, a cached target, and conservative fall-through on miss.\"\n\n(End of file - total 26 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260516-003-r11s2\ntitle: \"Retired loop-backedge predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  CoreMark still burns cycles on the same hot loop backedges, but the\n  broader predictor attempts paid too much in IF logic or speculative\n  state. A tiny predictor anchored to retired control-flow state is the\n  narrowest remaining way to hide those fetch bubbles without changing\n  the architectural redirect contract.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a single-entry loop-backedge predictor that remembers the most\n  recent retired taken conditional branch PC and target, then speculates\n  only on exact PC hits for backward branches. Train it strictly from\n  retired branch outcomes, keep EX-stage redirect authoritative for every\n  recovery path, and avoid any extra speculative training state so the\n  predictor stays small enough to help CoreMark without dragging Fmax.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r11s2.yaml","time":{"start":1778933716484,"end":1778933716540}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_02a91706242dda89016a085fd40d8c819a8d647a947d462f95"}},"id":"prt_e30b654f1001D592kdT9wSDF3J","sessionID":"ses_1cf4ad4ceffec3VftqnhrCFev2","messageID":"msg_e30b6430e001gVU286X5nqPS3O"}}
