{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778907911134,"sessionID":"ses_1d0d5ce71ffehNsS7Rr1i7GOzE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_2g5WuA5YV9QgL6FzZk5ijba8","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r6s2.yaml","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r6s2.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260516-003-r6s2\n2: title: \"Advisory loop-backedge predictor\"\n3: category: predictor\n4: motivation: |\n5:   CoreMark still spends cycles on repeated loop backedges and direct jumps,\n6:   so the core keeps paying the EX-stage fetch bubble on control transfers\n7:   that are cheap to predict statically. A predictor with no training state\n8:   is the lowest-risk way to hide more of that control-flow latency.\n9: hypothesis: |\n10:   Add a purely combinational BTFNT-style hint in IF: predict direct JALs\n11:   taken and predict conditional branches taken only when the immediate is\n12:   backward, while forward branches fall through. Keep EX-stage resolution\n13:   as the architectural source of truth for redirects and mispredict repair,\n14:   so the predictor only changes speculative fetch and not RVFI behavior.\n15: expected_impact:\n16:   fitness_delta_pct: 4\n17:   confidence: medium\n18: changes:\n19:   - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n20:     description: \"Add a stateless static branch-direction hint in fetch, but leave EX redirects and wrong-path squashing authoritative.\"\n\n(End of file - total 20 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260516-003-r6s2\ntitle: \"Advisory loop-backedge predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  CoreMark still spends cycles on repeated loop backedges and direct jumps,\n  so the core keeps paying the EX-stage fetch bubble on control transfers\n  that are cheap to predict statically. A predictor with no training state\n  is the lowest-risk way to hide more of that control-flow latency.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a purely combinational BTFNT-style hint in IF: predict direct JALs\n  taken and predict conditional branches taken only when the immediate is\n  backward, while forward branches fall through. Keep EX-stage resolution\n  as the architectural source of truth for redirects and mispredict repair,\n  so the predictor only changes speculative fetch and not RVFI behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a stateless static branch-direction hint in fetch, but leave EX redirects and wrong-path squashing authoritative.\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r6s2.yaml","time":{"start":1778907911099,"end":1778907911133}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0f192937f597c127016a07fb06f48c819b937de48d1ac153f4"}},"id":"prt_e2f2c93b40012iUkjc5ekytVAK","sessionID":"ses_1d0d5ce71ffehNsS7Rr1i7GOzE","messageID":"msg_e2f2c8638001AVyKeQ7b1ilcpa"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778907911147,"sessionID":"ses_1d0d5ce71ffehNsS7Rr1i7GOzE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_13sRJCry5GMUPtYqf2Zb442o","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r6s0.yaml","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r6s0.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260516-001-r6s0\n2: title: \"Operand-use hazard gating\"\n3: category: micro_opt\n4: motivation: |\n5:   The core already predecodes opcode and register slices, but the hazard\n6:   and forwarding logic still compares raw rs fields for every instruction.\n7:   That creates avoidable compare fanout and can also stall on rs2 bits that\n8:   are really immediates in single-source instructions.\n9: hypothesis: |\n10:   Add predecoded operand-use flags so the pipe only compares rs1/rs2 when\n11:   the current instruction actually reads them. Carry those flags through\n12:   IF/ID and ID/EX, then gate load-use detection and EX forwarding selects\n13:   with them to remove spurious stalls and trim hot compare logic without\n14:   changing RVFI or retirement behavior.\n15: expected_impact:\n16:   fitness_delta_pct: 4\n17:   confidence: medium\n18: changes:\n19:   - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n20:     description: \"Extend the pipeline bundles with operand-use bits for rs1/rs2 so downstream hazard and forwarding logic can ignore unused source fields.\"\n21:   - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n22:     description: \"Predecode which source operands are actually read and carry those bits alongside the fetched instruction.\"\n23:   - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n24:     description: \"Latch the operand-use flags into ID/EX so execute-side forwarding can skip irrelevant source compares.\"\n25:   - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n26:     description: \"Gate load-use checks with the operand-use flags to avoid false stalls on immediate and single-source instructions.\"\n27:   - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n28:     description: \"Use the operand-use flags to prune unnecessary rs compare logic in the EX-stage forwarding network.\"\n\n(End of file - total 28 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260516-001-r6s0\ntitle: \"Operand-use hazard gating\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The core already predecodes opcode and register slices, but the hazard\n  and forwarding logic still compares raw rs fields for every instruction.\n  That creates avoidable compare fanout and can also stall on rs2 bits that\n  are really immediates in single-source instructions.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add predecoded operand-use flags so the pipe only compares rs1/rs2 when\n  the current instruction actually reads them. Carry those flags through\n  IF/ID and ID/EX, then gate load-use detection and EX forwarding selects\n  with them to remove spurious stalls and trim hot compare logic without\n  changing RVFI or retirement behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Extend the pipeline bundles with operand-use bits for rs1/rs2 so downstream hazard and forwarding logic can ignore unused source fields.\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r6s0.yaml","time":{"start":1778907911089,"end":1778907911136}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0f192937f597c127016a07fb06f47c819bba7d8f3f732859c4"}},"id":"prt_e2f2c939d001OM9OH8uRsYVMa7","sessionID":"ses_1d0d5ce71ffehNsS7Rr1i7GOzE","messageID":"msg_e2f2c8638001AVyKeQ7b1ilcpa"}}
