{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778912293177,"sessionID":"ses_1d0910fb0ffeHm1SXpsYV2gloX","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_h579MZUfck8qqhQ1BIpNtF1i","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r7s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-002-r7s1\n+title: \"Richer predecode for decode fanout\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The last structural win came from shrinking the instruction fanout into\n+  decode. There is still more repeated opcode/funct classification on the hot\n+  IF/ID -> ID/EX path, and that work can be hoisted earlier without changing\n+  retirement or trap behavior.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Extend the IF-stage predecode bundle with compact instruction-class and\n+  legality bits so ID no longer rebuilds those classifications from the raw\n+  32-bit instruction on every cycle. This should trim another slice of decode\n+  fanout and case-tree depth while leaving the architectural control flow,\n+  RVFI contract, and memory behavior unchanged.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add compact instruction-class / legality fields to the predecode and pipeline bundles.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute the richer predecode metadata once at fetch time and carry it forward with the instruction.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consume the predecoded instruction-class bits instead of rebuilding opcode/funct legality from scratch.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Simplify decode dispatch so it consumes the hoisted classification data without changing legality rules.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r7s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores