patch so it consumes the hoisted classification data without changing legality rules.\"\n\n(End of file - total 26 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260516-002-r7s1\ntitle: \"Richer predecode for decode fanout\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The last structural win came from shrinking the instruction fanout into\n  decode. There is still more repeated opcode/funct classification on the hot\n  IF/ID -> ID/EX path, and that work can be hoisted earlier without changing\n  retirement or trap behavior.\nhypothesis: |\n  Extend the IF-stage predecode bundle with compact instruction-class and\n  legality bits so ID no longer rebuilds those classifications from the raw\n  32-bit instruction on every cycle. This should trim another slice of decode\n  fanout and case-tree depth while leaving the architectural control flow,\n  RVFI contract, and memory behavior unchanged.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add compact instruction-class / legality fields to the predecode and pipeline bundles.\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r7s1.yaml","time":{"start":1778912298005,"end":1778912298027}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0a16496f69888765016a080c29b3488198b32060518d64ca6c"}},"id":"prt_e2f6f835b001n2ZHOUs65SExmU","sessionID":"ses_1d0910fb0ffeHm1SXpsYV2gloX","messageID":"msg_e2f6f72dc001TBCBDeBKnpr6jp"}}
