IF/ID -> ID/EX path\\nwithout changing any architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a compact predecode bundle in IF that latches opcode, funct3/funct7,\\nrd/rs1/rs2, and the already-formed immediate fragments, then have ID use\\nthose narrow fields instead of re-slicing the raw instruction everywhere.\\nThis is a structural timing cleanup aimed at reducing the decode-critical\\npath and top-level instruction fanout while keeping RVFI, traps, and\\nretirement order unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a compact predecode bundle to carry opcode/funct and register slices through IF/ID.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Capture the predecode bundle alongside the fetched instruction so downstream logic sees narrow fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the predecoded slices instead of repeatedly extracting them from the full instruction word.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor decode to operate on predecoded opcode/funct inputs while keeping legality checks unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/imm_gen.sv\", \"description\": \"Optionally source immediate fragments from the predecode bundle to shorten decode fanout.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl...\n  Line 17: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r6s0\", \"title\": \"Operand-use hazard gating\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The core already predecodes opcode and register slices, but the hazard\\nand forwarding logic still compares raw rs fields for every instruction.\\nThat creates avoidable compare fanout and can also stall on rs2 bits that\\nare really immediates in single-source instructions.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The core already predecodes opcode and register slices, but the hazard\\nand forwarding logic still compares raw rs fields for every instruction.\\nThat creates avoidable compare fanout and can also stall on rs2 bits that\\nare really immediates in single-source instructions.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add predecoded operand-use flags so the pipe only compares rs1/rs2 when\\nthe current instruction actually reads them. Carry those flags through\\nIF/ID and ID/EX, then gate load-use detection and EX forwarding selects\\nwith them to remove spurious stalls and trim hot compare logic without\\nchanging RVFI or retirement behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the pipeline bundles with operand-use bits for rs1/rs2 so downstream hazard and forwarding logic can ignore unused source fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Predecode which source operands are actually read and carry those bits alongside the fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the operand-use flags into ID/EX so execute-side forwarding can skip irrelevant source compares.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use checks with the operand-use flags to avoid false stalls on immediate and single-source instructions.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the operand-use flags to prune unnecessary rs compare logic in the EX-stage forwarding network.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"c...\n  Line 18: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r6s1\", \"title\": \"(slot 1 hypothesis-gen failed)\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"hypothesis_gen_failed: Hypothesis agent modified off-limits paths and was rolled back: ['cores/bench/rtl/core.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv']\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 6, \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark is heavy on loads and stores, and `mem_stage.sv` still recomputes\\nbyte masks, address alignment, and load shift behavior from `alu_result`\\nand `mem_width` on every memory op. Moving that address-derived metadata\\nearlier should shorten the hot memory path and reduce fanout without\\nchanging any architectural results.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add precomputed memory-lane metadata to the EX/MEM bundle: word-aligned\\naddress, byte mask, shift amount, and misalignment status. Have\\n`ex_stage.sv` derive those fields once from `alu_result[1:0]` and\\n`mem_width`, then let `mem_stage.sv` consume them directly so it only\\ngates the bus and forms the final load value. This is a structural\\ncleanup aimed at trimming the memory-access critical path while keeping\\nRVFI, traps, and retirement order unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the EX/MEM bundle with precomputed memory-lane metadata such as aligned address, byte mask, shift amount, and misalign flag.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive the memory-lane metadata once from the ALU result and load/store width before the MEM stage.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the precomputed lane metadata so the memory stage no longer repeats width-based mask, alignment, and shift logic.\"}]}, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-002-r6s1 (broken, n/a): Structural hot-path cleanup onl...\n  Line 20: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r7s0\", \"title\": \"Operand-use compare gating\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on instructions that do not read both\\nsource registers. The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares\\nraw rs fields unconditionally, which adds fanout on the hot decode path\\nand can also create avoidable load-use stalls on immediate-style ops.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on instructions that do not read both\\nsource registers. The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares\\nraw rs fields unconditionally, which adds fanout on the hot decode path\\nand can also create avoidable load-use stalls on immediate-style ops.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Predecode `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` once in IF, carry those bits through\\nIF/ID and ID/EX, and use them to short-circuit the forwarding and\\nload-use compare trees. This should trim always-on compare logic from the\\nhottest control path while preserving RVFI, trap behavior, and in-order\\nretirement.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add operand-use flags to the predecode and pipeline bundles so source-register activity is tracked explicitly.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` from the fetched opcode class and latch them with the predecoded instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the operand-use flags into ID/EX alongside the decoded control bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use detection with the operand-use flags so instructions that do not read rs2 do not trigger false stalls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the operand-use flags to prune unnecessary rs compare logic in the EX-stage forwarding network.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"descript...\n  Line 21: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r7s1\", \"title\": \"Richer predecode for decode fanout\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The last structural win came from shrinking the instruction fanout into\\ndecode. There is still more repeated opcode/funct classification on the hot\\nIF/ID -> ID/EX path, and that work can be hoisted earlier without changing\\nretirement or trap behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The last structural win came from shrinking the instruction fanout into\\ndecode. There is still more repeated opcode/funct classification on the hot\\nIF/ID -> ID/EX path, and that work can be hoisted earlier without changing\\nretirement or trap behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Extend the IF-stage predecode bundle with compact instruction-class and\\nlegality bits so ID no longer rebuilds those classifications from the raw\\n32-bit instruction on every cycle. This should trim another slice of decode\\nfanout and case-tree depth while leaving the architectural control flow,\\nRVFI contract, and memory behavior unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add compact instruction-class / legality fields to the predecode and pipeline bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the richer predecode metadata once at fetch time and carry it forward with the instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the predecoded instruction-class bits instead of rebuilding opcode/funct legality from scratch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Simplify decode dispatch so it consumes the hoisted classification data without changing legality rules.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add compact instruction-class / legality fields to the predecode and pipeline bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the richer predecode metadata once ...","metadata":{"matches":12,"truncated":false},"title":"\"category\": \"structural\"|