": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Capture the predecode bundle alongside the fetched instruction so downstream logic sees narrow fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the predecoded slices instead of repeatedly extracting them from the full instruction word.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor decode to operate on predecoded opcode/funct inputs while keeping legality checks unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/imm_gen.sv\", \"description\": \"Optionally source immediate fragments from the predecode bundle to shorten decode fanout.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n16: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r5s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny branch-direction predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends cycles waiting on repeated control transfers, especially\\nshort loop backedges and recurring direct jumps. A very small predictor that\\nlearns branch direction without general BTB state could hide those bubbles\\nwhile keeping the existing EX redirect path as the architectural source of\\ntruth.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends cycles waiting on repeated control transfers, especially\\nshort loop backedges and recurring direct jumps. A very small predictor that\\nlearns branch direction without general BTB state could hide those bubbles\\nwhile keeping the existing EX redirect path as the architectural source of\\ntruth.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny direct-mapped direction predictor in IF that speculatively chooses\\nbetween fall-through and the already-available control-flow target, while EX\\nresolution remains authoritative for recovery. Keep the state to a few\\nlearned taken/not-taken bits so repeated CoreMark branches can settle quickly\\nwithout the formal and timing cost of a full BTB or return-stack design.\\n\", \"expected_impact