delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the pipeline bundles with operand-use bits for rs1/rs2 so downstream hazard and forwarding logic can ignore unused source fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Predecode which source operands are actually read and carry those bits alongside the fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the operand-use flags into ID/EX so execute-side forwarding can skip irrelevant source compares.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use checks with the operand-use flags to avoid false stalls on immediate and single-source instructions.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the operand-use flags to prune unnecessary rs compare logic in the EX-stage forwarding network.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"c... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n18: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r6s1\", \"title\": \"(slot 1 hypothesis-gen failed)\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"hypothesis_gen_failed: Hypothesis agent modified off-limits paths and was rolled back: ['cores/bench/rtl/core.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv']\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 6, \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark is heavy on loads and stores, and `mem_stage.sv` still recomputes\\nbyte masks, address alignment, and load shift behavior from `alu_result`\\nand `mem_width` on every memory op. Moving that address-derived metadata\\nearlier should shorten the hot memory path and reduce fanout without\\nchanging any architectural results.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add precomputed memory-lane metadata to the EX/MEM bundle: word-aligned\\naddress, byte mask, shift amount, and misalignment status. Have\\n`ex_stage.sv` derive those fields once from `alu_result[1:0]` and\\n`mem_width`, then let `mem_stage.sv` consume them directly so it only\\ngates the bus and forms the final load value. This is a structural\\ncleanup aimed at trimming the memory-access critical path while keeping\\nRVFI, traps, and retirement order unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the EX/MEM bundle with precomputed memory-lane metadata such as aligned address, byte mask, shift amount, and misalign flag.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive the memory-lane metadata once from the ALU result and load/store width before the MEM stage.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the precomputed lane metadata so the memory stage no longer repeats width-based mask, alignment, and shift logic.\"}]}, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-002-r6s1 (broken, n/a): Structural hot-path cleanup onl... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n19: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r6s2\", \"title\": \"Advisory loop-backedge predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends cycles on repeated loop backedges and direct jumps,\\nso the core keeps paying the EX-stage fetch bubble on control transfers\\nthat are cheap to predict statically. A predictor with no training state\\nis the lowest-risk way to hide more of that control-flow latency.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends cycles on repeated loop backedges and direct jumps,\\nso the core keeps paying the EX-stage fetch bubble on control transfers\\nthat are cheap to predict statically. A predictor with no training state\\nis the lowest-risk way to hide more of that control-flow latency.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a purely combinational BTFNT-style hint in IF: predict direct JALs\\ntaken and predict conditional branches taken only when the immediate is\\nbackward, while forward branches fall through. Keep EX-stage resolution\\nas the architectural source of truth for redirects and mispredict repair,\\nso the predictor only changes speculative fetch and not RVFI behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a stateless static branch-direction hint in fetch, but leave EX redirects and wrong-path squashing authoritative.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a stateless static branch-direction hint in fetch, but leave EX redirects and wrong-path squashing authoritative.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 294.69, \"delta_pct\": -8.75, \"vs_baseline\": 4.2, \"fmax_mhz\": 125.53, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4259699, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10478, \"ff\": 1929, \"seeds\": [127.75, 125.53, 122.74], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-16T06:16:34.091429Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n20: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r7s0\", \"title\": \"Operand-use compare gating\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on instructions that do not read both\\nsource registers. The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares\\nraw rs fields unconditionally, which adds fanout on the hot decode path\\nand can also create avoidable load-use stalls on immediate-style ops.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on instructions that do not read both\\nsource registers. The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares\\nraw rs fields unconditionally, which adds fanout on the hot decode path\\nand can also create avoidable load-use stalls on immediate-style ops.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Predecode `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` once in IF, carry those bits through\\nIF/ID and ID/EX, and use them to short-circuit the forwarding and\\nload-use compare trees. This should trim always-on compare logic from the\\nhottest control path while preserving RVFI, trap behavior, and in-order\\nretirement.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add operand-use flags to the predecode and pipeline bundles so source-register activity is tracked explicitly.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` from the fetched opcode class and latch them with the predecoded instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the operand-use flags into ID/EX alongside the decoded control bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use detection with the operand-use flags so instructions that do not read rs2 do not trigger false stalls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the operand-use flags to prune unnecessary rs compare logic in the EX-stage forwarding network.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"descript... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n21: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r7s1\", \"title\": \"Richer predecode for decode fanout\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The last structural win came from shrinking the instruction fanout into\\ndecode. There is still more repeated opcode/funct classification on the hot\\nIF/ID -> ID/EX path, and that work can be hoisted earlier without changing\\nretirement or trap behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The last structural win came from shrinking the instruction fanout into\\ndecode. There is still more repeated opcode/funct classification on the hot\\nIF/ID -> ID/EX path, and that work can be hoisted earlier without changing\\nretirement or trap behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Extend the IF-stage predecode bundle with compact instruction-class and\\nlegality bits so ID no longer rebuilds those classifications from the raw\\n32-bit instruction on every cycle. This should trim another slice of decode\\nfanout and case-tree depth while leaving the architectural control flow,\\nRVFI contract, and memory behavior unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add compact instruction-class / legality fields to the predecode and pipeline bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the richer predecode metadata once at fetch time and carry it forward with the instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the predecoded instruction-class bits instead of rebuilding opcode/funct legality from scratch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Simplify decode dispatch so it consumes the hoisted classification data without changing legality rules.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add compact instruction-class / legality fields to the predecode and pipeline bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the richer predecode metadata once ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n22: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r7s2\", \"title\": \"Single-entry loop predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark has hot loop backedges that repeat many times, but the prior\\nbroader predictors paid too much cost in IF logic and formal complexity.\\nA one-entry loop cache should capture the dominant repeat without the\\ntraining and state overhead of a general BTB or return stack.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark has hot loop backedges that repeat many times, but the prior\\nbroader predictors paid too much cost in IF logic and formal complexity.\\nA one-entry loop cache should capture the dominant repeat without the\\ntraining and state overhead of a general BTB or return stack.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a single-entry loop predictor in IF that remembers the last taken\\nconditional backedge's PC and target, and speculatively redirects only on\\na tag hit. Train it only from resolved EX outcomes, keep EX redirect\\nauthoritative on every miss or mismatch, and avoid speculative training\\nstate beyond that one cached loop target.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume a tiny loop-predictor hint for speculative next-PC selection, but always yield to EX-stage redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire resolved branch outcomes into the predictor update path without changing the RVFI or trap contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a single-entry tagged loop-target cache with conservative fall-through on miss and update-on-resolved-branch behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume a tiny loop-predictor hint for speculative next-PC selection, but always yield to EX-stage redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire resolved branch outcomes into the predictor update path without changing the RV... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n\n(End of file - total 22 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-2a72da6\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 282.82, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 127.03, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9563, \"ff\": 1866, \"seeds\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-15T23:18:18.323525Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Zero-wait load bypass\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark is load-heavy, and the current 5-stage pipe pays a full bubble\\non every load-use pair even when the data memory is zero-wait. Removing\\nthat unnecessary interlock should raise iterations per cycle without\\nchanging the ISA or the top-level RVFI contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark is load-heavy, and the current 5-stage pipe pays a full bubble\\non every load-use pair even when the data memory is zero-wait. Removing\\nthat unnecessary interlock should raise iterations per cycle without\\nchanging the ISA or the top-level RVFI contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a combinational MEM-to-EX bypass for load results so a dependent\\ninstruction can consume the loaded word in the next cycle instead of\\nstalling behind the load. Keep the existing dmem backpressure stall\\npath intact, but stop treating zero-wait load-use pairs as mandatory\\nbubbles.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the combinational load result and metadata needed for a same-cycle bypass.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a forwarding input that can source operands directly from the current MEM-stage load data.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Relax the load-use interlock when the zero-wait MEM bypass can satisfy the dependency.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the new MEM-stage bypass signals through the pipeline.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the combinational load result and metadata needed for a same-cycle bypass.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a forwarding input that can source operands directly from the current MEM-stage load data.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Relax the load-use inter... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Precompute branch targets in ID\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current EX stage computes both the branch condition and the 32-bit\\nPC+imm target in the same cycle. Moving the target add upstream should\\nshorten the EX critical path and is a low-risk structural change for a\\nbranch-heavy CoreMark workload.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current EX stage computes both the branch condition and the 32-bit\\nPC+imm target in the same cycle. Moving the target add upstream should\\nshorten the EX critical path and is a low-risk structural change for a\\nbranch-heavy CoreMark workload.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a `branch_target` field to the ID/EX bundle, compute B-type targets\\nin `id_stage.sv`, and have `ex_stage.sv` reuse that precomputed target\\ninstead of redoing `pc + imm` in EX. This preserves the retirement and\\ntrap contract while trimming one adder from the execute-side timing path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the ID/EX bundle with a latched branch-target field.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Precompute branch targets during decode and store them in the pipeline register.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the latched branch target and remove the EX-side branch-target adder.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the ID/EX bundle with a latched branch-target field.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Precompute branch targets during decode and store them in the pipeline register.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the latched branch target and remove the EX-side branch-target adder.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 296.38, \"delta_pct\": 4.79, \"vs_baseline\": 4.79, \"fmax_mhz\": 133.12, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterat... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny BTB loop predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time in short loops and repeated call/return\\npaths, so this core is paying the full EX-stage branch penalty on the\\nsame control transfers over and over. A very small predictor should\\nremove those bubbles with limited area cost and without changing the\\nin-order retirement contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time in short loops and repeated call/return\\npaths, so this core is paying the full EX-stage branch penalty on the\\nsame control transfers over and over. A very small predictor should\\nremove those bubbles with limited area cost and without changing the\\nin-order retirement contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a compact direct-mapped branch target buffer with 2-bit saturating\\ncounters and use it to speculatively redirect fetch on hot taken\\nbranches and jump targets from IF. Keep EX-stage resolution as the\\narchitectural source of truth so mispredict recovery stays simple and\\nthe RVFI / trap behavior remains unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread speculative next-PC selection through fetch and fall back to the existing redirect path on mispredicts.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate and connect the predictor update path using EX-stage resolution signals.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small direct-mapped BTB with 2-bit counters and update logic for taken branches and jumps.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread speculative next-PC selection through fetch and fall back to the existing redirect path on mispredicts.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate and connect the predictor update path using EX-stage resolution signals.\"}, {\"fi... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Resolve branches in ID\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"Branch-heavy CoreMark spends a lot of time paying the taken-branch\\nbubble created by waiting until EX to know the outcome. Moving the\\ncommon conditional-branch decision into ID should cut one wrong-path\\ncycle while also shortening the EX timing cone.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Branch-heavy CoreMark spends a lot of time paying the taken-branch\\nbubble created by waiting until EX to know the outcome. Moving the\\ncommon conditional-branch decision into ID should cut one wrong-path\\ncycle while also shortening the EX timing cone.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add local operand forwarding into ID so BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU can\\nbe resolved as soon as decode has the operands, using the branch target\\nalready precomputed in ID. Keep EX as the architectural fallback for\\nthe remaining jump/misalign cases, but stop burning a full EX-stage\\nbubble on ordinary taken branches.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the pipeline bundle with any extra ID-side branch resolve state needed for early branch handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add branch compare logic and local forwarding so common conditional branches can resolve in decode.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Teach the hazard logic when an ID-resolved branch still needs a stall versus when it can redirect immediately.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the new ID-stage branch decision into fetch/redirect control without changing the RVFI contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the pipeline bundle with any extra ID-side branch resolve state needed for early branch handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add branch compare logic and local forwarding... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r2s1\", \"title\": \"Latch pc+4 in ID\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The execute stage still rebuilds the sequential fall-through PC in the hot\\nretirement path, even though that value is known as soon as the IF/ID PC is\\nlatched. Hoisting that adder out of EX should trim a little more logic from\\nthe branch/link critical path without changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The execute stage still rebuilds the sequential fall-through PC in the hot\\nretirement path, even though that value is known as soon as the IF/ID PC is\\nlatched. Hoisting that adder out of EX should trim a little more logic from\\nthe branch/link critical path without changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a latched `pc_plus4` field to the ID/EX bundle, compute it in\\n`id_stage.sv`, and have `ex_stage.sv` reuse that precomputed value for JAL\\nlink writeback and fall-through `pc_next` selection. This is a structural\\ntiming cleanup: it removes another 32-bit add from EX while