{"type":"text","timestamp":1778919296305,"sessionID":"ses_1d02649b0ffeegxIcj9zf3QCr9","part":{"id":"prt_e2fda4d0e001lsoESUQ6yKXdgp","messageID":"msg_e2fda0cea001E7k0RiUBFKsDZh","sessionID":"ses_1d02649b0ffeegxIcj9zf3QCr9","type":"text","text":"I’ve got the best remaining structural angle: move memory-lane derivation out of `mem_stage` so the hot load/store path does less width/alignment work per access. I’m writing that as the hypothesis now.","time":{"start":1778919296270,"end":1778919296300},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_041103fbb2b60777016a082780100c81988d40b44fcdafe600","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778919297464,"sessionID":"ses_1d02649b0ffeegxIcj9zf3QCr9","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_zVHZcGl8qhd6lQdaW9JG4liN","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r8s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-002-r8s1\n+title: \"Move memory lane work earlier\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark is still heavy on loads and stores, and the current MEM stage\n+  recomputes byte masks, alignment, and shift selection from `alu_result`\n+  on every access. Hoisting that address-lane work earlier should shorten\n+  the hot memory path and reduce fanout without changing architectural\n+  behavior.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Extend the EX/MEM bundle with precomputed memory-lane metadata such as\n+  the aligned address, byte mask, shift amount, and misalign flag, then\n+  have `ex_stage.sv` derive those fields once from `alu_result` and\n+  `mem_width` before `mem_stage.sv` consumes them directly. This keeps the\n+  RVFI, trap, and retirement contract unchanged while trimming redundant\n+  width-based logic from the memory-access critical path.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Extend the EX/MEM bundle with precomputed memory-lane metadata for address alignment, byte masking, and shift control.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Derive and latch the memory-lane metadata once from the ALU result and load/store width before the MEM stage.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consume the precomputed lane metadata so the memory stage no longer repeats width-based mask, alignment, and shift logic.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r8s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_