{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778925114589,"sessionID":"ses_1cfcdc69affeyfg4TwH0EtEGsf","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_5G87kbTkWrZkppX1qmKRrB5E","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r9s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-002-r9s1\n+title: \"One-hot decode classes\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The hot decode path still rebuilds opcode/funct legality and instruction\n+  class information from the raw 32-bit instruction in ID. Hoisting that\n+  classification into fetch-time predecode should cut repeated case-tree\n+  work and narrow the control fanout seen by the rest of the pipe.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add compact one-hot instruction-class metadata to the IF-stage predecode\n+  bundle, then have ID consume those cached classes when forming control and\n+  hazard inputs instead of repeatedly re-decoding the same opcode/funct\n+  patterns from `instr[31:0]`. Keep the decoder's legality rules unchanged,\n+  but make the common control path structurally narrower so EX and MEM see\n+  less combinational decode work on every cycle.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Extend the predecode and pipeline bundles with compact one-hot instruction-class metadata.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute and latch the instruction-class metadata once at fetch time.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consume the predecoded classes when building control signals instead of re-decoding from the full instruction word.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Keep legality semantics identical while simplifying dispatch around the predecoded instruction class inputs.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r9s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users