latched `jalr_target` field to the ID/EX bundle and compute the\\nJALR destination in `id_stage.sv` from the decoded immediate plus a\\nforwarded rs1 value, then have `ex_stage.sv` use the precomputed target\\nfor redirect and misalignment checks. This keeps EX as the architectural\\nresolve point but removes the remaining JALR add/mux from its timing path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a latched `jalr_target` field to the ID/EX bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the forwarding information needed for an ID-side JALR target precompute.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Precompute and latch the JALR target alongside the existing decode metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the latched JALR target and remove the EX-side `rs1 + imm` adder.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the new JALR precompute path through the top-level pipeline.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a latched `jalr_target` field to the ID/EX bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the forwardi...\n  Line 13: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r4s2\", \"title\": \"Advisory BTFNT fetch hint\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends a lot of time in tight loops and repeated control\\ntransfers, so the core keeps paying the EX-stage branch bubble on paths\\nthat are easy to predict statically. A predictor with no training state\\nshould be cheap enough for this tiny FPGA core.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends a lot of time in tight loops and repeated control\\ntransfers, so the core keeps paying the EX-stage branch bubble on paths\\nthat are easy to predict statically. A predictor with no training state\\nshould be cheap enough for this tiny FPGA core.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Fold a purely combinational BTFNT hint into IF: predict backward\\nconditional branches taken, forward conditional branches not taken, and\\ndirect JALs taken. Keep EX redirect as the architectural source of truth\\nso mispredict recovery stays simple and RVFI/trap behavior is unchanged,\\nbut hide more fetch bubbles on CoreMark's hot loops.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a stateless static branch-direction predictor that chooses the speculative next PC while still yielding to EX-stage redirects.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a stateless static branch-direction predictor that chooses the speculative next PC while still yielding to EX-stage redirects.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: insn_beq_ch0\\nsummary: counterexample trace: insn_blt_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY  0:18:39 [insn_blt_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_insn_check_sv_178_115 at rvfi_insn_check.sv:178.7-178.76 step 20\\nSBY  0:18:39 [insn_blt_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\nSBY  0:22:11 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ...\n  Line 16: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r5s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny branch-direction predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends cycles waiting on repeated control transfers, especially\\nshort loop backedges and recurring direct jumps. A very small predictor that\\nlearns branch direction without general BTB state could hide those bubbles\\nwhile keeping the existing EX redirect path as the architectural source of\\ntruth.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends cycles waiting on repeated control transfers, especially\\nshort loop backedges and recurring direct jumps. A very small predictor that\\nlearns branch direction without general BTB state could hide those bubbles\\nwhile keeping the existing EX redirect path as the architectural source of\\ntruth.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny direct-mapped direction predictor in IF that speculatively chooses\\nbetween fall-through and the already-available control-flow target, while EX\\nresolution remains authoritative for recovery. Keep the state to a few\\nlearned taken/not-taken bits so repeated CoreMark branches can settle quickly\\nwithout the formal and timing cost of a full BTB or return-stack design.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use predictor output to select the speculative next PC before EX resolution, but keep EX redirects as the final authority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire resolved branch outcome information into the predictor update path without changing RVFI or trap behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny direct-mapped branch-direction table with simple update logic and a conservative fallback to fall-through.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use predictor output to select the speculative next PC before EX resolution, but keep EX redirects as the ...\n  Line 19: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r6s2\", \"title\": \"Advisory loop-backedge predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends cycles on repeated loop backedges and direct jumps,\\nso the core keeps paying the EX-stage fetch bubble on control transfers\\nthat are cheap to predict statically. A predictor with no training state\\nis the lowest-risk way to hide more of that control-flow latency.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends cycles on repeated loop backedges and direct jumps,\\nso the core keeps paying the EX-stage fetch bubble on control transfers\\nthat are cheap to predict statically. A predictor with no training state\\nis the lowest-risk way to hide more of that control-flow latency.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a purely combinational BTFNT-style hint in IF: predict direct JALs\\ntaken and predict conditional branches taken only when the immediate is\\nbackward, while forward branches fall through. Keep EX-stage resolution\\nas the architectural source of truth for redirects and mispredict repair,\\nso the predictor only changes speculative fetch and not RVFI behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a stateless static branch-direction hint in fetch, but leave EX redirects and wrong-path squashing authoritative.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a stateless static branch-direction hint in fetch, but leave EX redirects and wrong-path squashing authoritative.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 294.69, \"delta_pct\": -8.75, \"vs_baseline\": 4.2, \"fmax_mhz\": 125.53, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4259699, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10478, \"ff\": 1929, \"seeds\": [127.75, 125.53, 122.74], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-16T06:16:34.091429Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson...\n  Line 22: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r7s2\", \"title\": \"Single-entry loop predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark has hot loop backedges that repeat many times, but the prior\\nbroader predictors paid too much cost in IF logic and formal complexity.\\nA one-entry loop cache should capture the dominant repeat without the\\ntraining and state overhead of a general BTB or return stack.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark has hot loop backedges that repeat many times, but the prior\\nbroader predictors paid too much cost in IF logic and formal complexity.\\nA one-entry loop cache should capture the dominant repeat without the\\ntraining and state overhead of a general BTB or return stack.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a single-entry loop predictor in IF that remembers the last taken\\nconditional backedge's PC and target, and speculatively redirects only on\\na tag hit. Train it only from resolved EX outcomes, keep EX redirect\\nauthoritative on every miss or mismatch, and avoid speculative training\\nstate beyond that one cached loop target.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume a tiny loop-predictor hint for speculative next-PC selection, but always yield to EX-stage redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire resolved branch outcomes into the predictor update path without changing the RVFI or trap contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a single-entry tagged loop-target cache with conservative fall-through on miss and update-on-resolved-branch behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume a tiny loop-predictor hint for speculative next-PC selection, but always yield to EX-stage redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire resolved branch outcomes into the predictor update path without changing the RV...\n  Line 25: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r8s2\", \"title\": \"Return-only stack predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark still pays a repeatable bubble on function returns, and the prior\\nbroader predictor attempts were too expensive in IF. A very small return\\nstack can target that hot path without adding full BTB logic or changing\\nthe architectural redirect source of truth.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark still pays a repeatable bubble on function returns, and the prior\\nbroader predictor attempts were too expensive in IF. A very small return\\nstack can target that hot path without adding full BTB logic or changing\\nthe architectural redirect source of truth.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny return-address stack that predicts only canonical JALR returns.\\nUpdate it from already-latched PC+4 on resolved calls, use it speculatively\\nonly when the fetched instruction decodes as a return, and keep EX-stage\\nredirection authoritative for recovery. By narrowing the predictor to\\nreturns only, the design should stay much cheaper than the earlier\\ncall/return predictor while still removing recurring control-flow bubbles.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the return-stack hint for speculative next-PC selection on canonical returns, but always yield to EX-stage redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire resolved call/return metadata and PC+4 into the predictor update path without changing RVFI or trap behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/return_stack.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny return-address stack and canonical return-classification logic.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the return-stack hint for speculative next-PC selection on canonical returns, but always yield to EX-stage redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire resolve...\n  Line 28: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r9s2\", \"title\":