{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778929922166,"sessionID":"ses_1cf840575ffex6HenLtj6HvPlw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_V2VnNaA94SPmkY9ODxKUYupJ","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl","offset":22,"limit":3},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n22: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r7s2\", \"title\": \"Single-entry loop predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark has hot loop backedges that repeat many times, but the prior\\nbroader predictors paid too much cost in IF logic and formal complexity.\\nA one-entry loop cache should capture the dominant repeat without the\\ntraining and state overhead of a general BTB or return stack.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark has hot loop backedges that repeat many times, but the prior\\nbroader predictors paid too much cost in IF logic and formal complexity.\\nA one-entry loop cache should capture the dominant repeat without the\\ntraining and state overhead of a general BTB or return stack.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a single-entry loop predictor in IF that remembers the last taken\\nconditional backedge's PC and target, and speculatively redirects only on\\na tag hit. Train it only from resolved EX outcomes, keep EX redirect\\nauthoritative on every miss or mismatch, and avoid speculative training\\nstate beyond that one cached loop target.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume a tiny loop-predictor hint for speculative next-PC selection, but always yield to EX-stage redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire resolved branch outcomes into the predictor update path without changing the RVFI or trap contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a single-entry tagged loop-target cache with conservative fall-through on miss and update-on-resolved-branch behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume a tiny loop-predictor hint for speculative next-PC selection, but always yield to EX-stage redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire resolved branch outcomes into the predictor update path without changing the RV... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n23: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r8s0\", \"title\": \"Decoder-aligned operand-use gating\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on instructions that do not actually read both\\nsource registers. The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares raw\\nrs fields unconditionally, which adds fanout on the hot control path and can\\nalso create avoidable load-use stalls on immediate-style ops.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on instructions that do not actually read both\\nsource registers. The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares raw\\nrs fields unconditionally, which adds fanout on the hot control path and can\\nalso create avoidable load-use stalls on immediate-style ops.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add exact `uses_rs1`/`uses_rs2` bits to the predecode and control path using\\nthe same opcode/funct classification as the decoder, then gate load-use\\ndetection and EX forwarding compares with those bits. That should remove\\nfalse stalls on single-source instructions and trim always-on compare logic\\nwithout changing RVFI, traps, or in-order retirement.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add source-operand-use fields to the predecode/control bundles and keep the classification shape shared across stages.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch the exact operand-use bits alongside the existing predecode metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Populate the same operand-use classification from the validated opcode/funct table so IF and decode stay aligned.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the operand-use bits into ID/EX so downstream logic can rely on the same source-operand semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use detection with the operand-use bits to avoid false stalls on instructions that do not read rs2.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n24: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r8s1\", \"title\": \"Move memory lane work earlier\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark is still heavy on loads and stores, and the current MEM stage\\nrecomputes byte masks, alignment, and shift selection from `alu_result`\\non every access. Hoisting that address-lane work earlier should shorten\\nthe hot memory path and reduce fanout without changing architectural\\nbehavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark is still heavy on loads and stores, and the current MEM stage\\nrecomputes byte masks, alignment, and shift selection from `alu_result`\\non every access. Hoisting that address-lane work earlier should shorten\\nthe hot memory path and reduce fanout without changing architectural\\nbehavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Extend the EX/MEM bundle with precomputed memory-lane metadata such as\\nthe aligned address, byte mask, shift amount, and misalign flag, then\\nhave `ex_stage.sv` derive those fields once from `alu_result` and\\n`mem_width` before `mem_stage.sv` consumes them directly. This keeps the\\nRVFI, trap, and retirement contract unchanged while trimming redundant\\nwidth-based logic from the memory-access critical path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the EX/MEM bundle with precomputed memory-lane metadata for address alignment, byte masking, and shift control.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive and latch the memory-lane metadata once from the ALU result and load/store width before the MEM stage.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the precomputed lane metadata so the memory stage no longer repeats width-based mask, alignment, and shift logic.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the EX/MEM bundle with precomputed memory-lane metadata for address alignment, byte masking, and shift control.\"... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n\n(Showing lines 22-24 of 28. Use offset=25 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r7s2\", \"title\": \"Single-entry loop predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark has hot loop backedges that repeat many times, but the prior\\nbroader predictors paid too much cost in IF logic and formal complexity.\\nA one-entry loop cache should capture the dominant repeat without the\\ntraining and state overhead of a general BTB or return stack.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark has hot loop backedges that repeat many times, but the prior\\nbroader predictors paid too much cost in IF logic and formal complexity.\\nA one-entry loop cache should capture the dominant repeat without the\\ntraining and state overhead of a general BTB or return stack.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a single-entry loop predictor in IF that remembers the last taken\\nconditional backedge's PC and target, and speculatively redirects only on\\na tag hit. Train it only from resolved EX outcomes, keep EX redirect\\nauthoritative on every miss or mismatch, and avoid speculative training\\nstate beyond that one cached loop target.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume a tiny loop-predictor hint for speculative next-PC selection, but always yield to EX-stage redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire resolved branch outcomes into the predictor update path without changing the RVFI or trap contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a single-entry tagged loop-target cache with conservative fall-through on miss and update-on-resolved-branch behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume a tiny loop-predictor hint for speculative next-PC selection, but always yield to EX-stage redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire resolved branch outcomes into the predictor update path without changing the RV... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r8s0\", \"title\": \"Decoder-aligned operand-use gating\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on instructions that do not actually read both\\nsource registers. The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares raw\\nrs fields unconditionally, which adds fanout on the hot control path and can\\nalso create avoidable load-use stalls on immediate-style ops.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on instructions that do not actually read both\\nsource registers. The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares raw\\nrs fields unconditionally, which adds fanout on the hot control path and can\\nalso create avoidable load-use stalls on immediate-style ops.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add exact `uses_rs1`/`uses_rs2` bits to the predecode and control path using\\nthe same opcode/funct classification as the decoder, then gate load-use\\ndetection and EX forwarding compares with those bits. That should remove\\nfalse stalls on single-source instructions and trim always-on compare logic\\nwithout changing RVFI, traps, or in-order retirement.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add source-operand-use fields to the predecode/control bundles and keep the classification shape shared across stages.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch the exact operand-use bits alongside the existing predecode metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Populate the same operand-use classification from the validated opcode/funct table so IF and decode stay aligned.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the operand-use bits into ID/EX so downstream logic can rely on the same source-operand semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use detection with the operand-use bits to avoid false stalls on instructions that do not read rs2.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r8s1\", \"title\": \"Move memory lane work earlier\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark is still heavy on loads and stores, and the current MEM stage\\nrecomputes byte masks, alignment, and shift selection from `alu_result`\\non every access. Hoisting that address-lane work earlier should shorten\\nthe hot memory path and reduce fanout without changing architectural\\nbehavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark is still heavy on loads and stores, and the current MEM stage\\nrecomputes byte masks, alignment, and shift selection from `alu_result`\\non every access. Hoisting that address-lane work earlier should shorten\\nthe hot memory path and reduce fanout without changing architectural\\nbehavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Extend the EX/MEM bundle with precomputed memory-lane metadata such as\\nthe aligned address, byte mask, shift amount, and misalign flag, then\\nhave `ex_stage.sv` derive those fields once from `alu_result` and\\n`mem_width` before `mem_stage.sv` consumes them directly. This keeps the\\nRVFI, trap, and retirement contract unchanged while trimming redundant\\nwidth-based logic from the memory-access critical path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the EX/MEM bundle with precomputed memory-lane metadata for address alignment, byte masking, and shift control.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive and latch the memory-lane metadata once from the ALU result and load/store width before the MEM stage.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the precomputed lane metadata so the memory stage no longer repeats width-based mask, alignment, and shift logic.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the EX/MEM bundle with precomputed memory-lane metadata for address alignment, byte masking, and shift control.\"... (line truncated to 2000 chars)","truncated":true,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl","time":{"start":1778929922007,"end":1778929922160}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0f08ef7a71728269016a0851019868819987bbfdca3bc90c01"}},"id":"prt_e307c6f74001hjG2pqiwktqo49","sessionID":"ses_1cf840575ffex6HenLtj6HvPlw","messageID":"msg_e307c524e001fBnCD0SrL7P2zn"}}
