{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778929949364,"sessionID":"ses_1cf840575ffex6HenLtj6HvPlw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_HNaHv5KptDFhzRWNXOy0O8un","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n -A 6 -B 2 \"\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260516-003-r7s2\\\"\" \"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","timeout":120000,"workdir":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2","description":"Shows full loop predictor log entry"},"output":"20-{\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r7s0\", \"title\": \"Operand-use compare gating\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on instructions that do not read both\\nsource registers. The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares\\nraw rs fields unconditionally, which adds fanout on the hot decode path\\nand can also create avoidable load-use stalls on immediate-style ops.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on instructions that do not read both\\nsource registers. The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares\\nraw rs fields unconditionally, which adds fanout on the hot decode path\\nand can also create avoidable load-use stalls on immediate-style ops.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Predecode `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` once in IF, carry those bits through\\nIF/ID and ID/EX, and use them to short-circuit the forwarding and\\nload-use compare trees. This should trim always-on compare logic from the\\nhottest control path while preserving RVFI, trap behavior, and in-order\\nretirement.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add operand-use flags to the predecode and pipeline bundles so source-register activity is tracked explicitly.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` from the fetched opcode class and latch them with the predecoded instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the operand-use flags into ID/EX alongside the decoded control bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use detection with the operand-use flags so instructions that do not read rs2 do not trigger false stalls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the operand-use flags to prune unnecessary rs compare logic in the EX-stage forwarding network.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add operand-use flags to the predecode and pipeline bundles so source-register activity is tracked explicitly.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` from the fetched opcode class and latch them with the predecoded instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the operand-use flags into ID/EX alongside the decoded control bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use detection with the operand-use flags so instructions that do not read rs2 do not trigger false stalls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the operand-use flags to prune unnecessary rs compare logic in the EX-stage forwarding network.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"cosim_failed: selftest.elf\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 7, \"scribe_skipped\": \"PermissionError: scribe touched off-limits paths and was rolled back: ['cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv']\"}\n21-{\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r7s1\", \"title\": \"Richer predecode for decode fanout\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The last structural win came from shrinking the instruction fanout into\\ndecode. There is still more repeated opcode/funct classification on the hot\\nIF/ID -> ID/EX path, and that work can be hoisted earlier without changing\\nretirement or trap behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The last structural win came from shrinking the instruction fanout into\\ndecode. There is still more repeated opcode/funct classification on the hot\\nIF/ID -> ID/EX path, and that work can be hoisted earlier without changing\\nretirement or trap behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Extend the IF-stage predecode bundle with compact instruction-class and\\nlegality bits so ID no longer rebuilds those classifications from the raw\\n32-bit instruction on every cycle. This should trim another slice of decode\\nfanout and case-tree depth while leaving the architectural control flow,\\nRVFI contract, and memory behavior unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add compact instruction-class / legality fields to the predecode and pipeline bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the richer predecode metadata once at fetch time and carry it forward with the instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the predecoded instruction-class bits instead of rebuilding opcode/funct legality from scratch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Simplify decode dispatch so it consumes the hoisted classification data without changing legality rules.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add compact instruction-class / legality fields to the predecode and pipeline bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the richer predecode metadata once at fetch time and carry it forward with the instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the predecoded instruction-class bits instead of rebuilding opcode/funct legality from scratch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Simplify decode dispatch so it consumes the hoisted classification data without changing legality rules.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"sandbox_violation: agent touched off-limits paths: ['cores/bench/test/_helpers.py']\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 7}\n22:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r7s2\", \"title\": \"Single-entry loop predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark has hot loop backedges that repeat many times, but the prior\\nbroader predictors paid too much cost in IF logic and formal complexity.\\nA one-entry loop cache should capture the dominant repeat without the\\ntraining and state overhead of a general BTB or return stack.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark has hot loop backedges that repeat many times, but the prior\\nbroader predictors paid too much cost in IF logic and formal complexity.\\nA one-entry loop cache should capture the dominant repeat without the\\ntraining and state overhead of a general BTB or return stack.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a single-entry loop predictor in IF that remembers the last taken\\nconditional backedge's PC and target, and speculatively redirects only on\\na tag hit. Train it only from resolved EX outcomes, keep EX redirect\\nauthoritative on every miss or mismatch, and avoid speculative training\\nstate beyond that one cached loop target.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume a tiny loop-predictor hint for speculative next-PC selection, but always yield to EX-stage redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire resolved branch outcomes into the predictor update path without changing the RVFI or trap contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a single-entry tagged loop-target cache with conservative fall-through on miss and update-o