 or return stack.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark has hot loop backedges that repeat many times, but the prior\\nbroader predictors paid too much cost in IF logic and formal complexity.\\nA one-entry loop cache should capture the dominant repeat without the\\ntraining and state overhead of a general BTB or return stack.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a single-entry loop predictor in IF that remembers the last taken\\nconditional backedge's PC and target, and speculatively redirects only on\\na tag hit. Train it only from resolved EX outcomes, keep EX redirect\\nauthoritative on every miss or mismatch, and avoid speculative training\\nstate beyond that one cached loop target.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume a tiny loop-predictor hint for speculative next-PC selection, but always yield to EX-stage redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire resolved branch outcomes into the predictor update path without changing the RVFI or trap contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a single-entry tagged loop-target cache with conservative fall-through on miss and update-on-resolved-branch behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume a tiny loop-predictor hint for speculative next-PC selection, but always yield to EX-stage redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire resolved branch outcomes into the predictor update path without changing the RVFI or trap contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a single-entry tagged loop-target cache with conservative fall-through on miss and update-on-resolved-branch behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 257.88, \"delta_pct\": -20.15, \"vs_baseline\": -8.82, \"fmax_mhz\": 111.2, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4312067, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10745, \"ff\": 2028, \"seeds\": [109.24, 120.8, 111.2], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-16T08:11:49.487187Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 7, \"scribe_skipped\": \"PermissionError: scribe rewrote /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/LESSONS.md instead of appending; reverted to prior content\"}\n23-{\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r8s0\", \"title\": \"Decoder-aligned operand-use gating\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on instructions that do not actually read both\\nsource registers. The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares raw\\nrs fields unconditionally, which adds fanout on the hot control path and can\\nalso create avoidable load-use stalls on immediate-style ops.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on instructions that do not actually read both\\nsource registers. The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares raw\\nrs fields unconditionally, which adds fanout on the hot control path and can\\nalso create avoidable load-use stalls on immediate-style ops.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add exact `uses_rs1`/`uses_rs2` bits to the predecode and control path using\\nthe same opcode/funct classification as the decoder, then gate load-use\\ndetection and EX forwarding compares with those bits. That should remove\\nfalse stalls on single-source instructions and trim always-on compare logic\\nwithout changing RVFI, traps, or in-order retirement.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add source-operand-use fields to the predecode/control bundles and keep the classification shape shared across stages.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch the exact operand-use bits alongside the existing predecode metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Populate the same operand-use classification from the validated opcode/funct table so IF and decode stay aligned.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the operand-use bits into ID/EX so downstream logic can rely on the same source-operand semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use detection with the operand-use bits to avoid false stalls on instructions that do not read rs2.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the operand-use bits to prune unnecessary rs compare logic in the forwarding network.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add source-operand-use fields to the predecode/control bundles and keep the classification shape shared across stages.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch the exact operand-use bits alongside the existing predecode metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Populate the same operand-use classification from the validated opcode/funct table so IF and decode stay aligned.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the operand-use bits into ID/EX so downstream logic can rely on the same source-operand semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use detection with the operand-use bits to avoid false stalls on instructions that do not read rs2.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the operand-use bits to prune unnecessary rs compare logic in the forwarding network.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"cosim_failed: selftest.elf\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-001-r8s0 (broken, n/a): Gating RVFI `rs1`/`rs2` fields with operand-use bits changes the architectural retirement trace, so that optimization is only safe if the cosim/ISS side agrees on zeroing unused source registers.\"}\n24-{\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r8s1\", \"title\": \"Move memory lane work earlier\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark is still heavy on loads and stores, and the current MEM stage\\nrecomputes byte masks, alignment, and shift selection from `alu_result`\\non every access. Hoisting that address-lane work earlier should shorten\\nthe hot memory path and reduce fanout without changing architectural\\nbehavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark is still heavy on loads and stores, and the current MEM stage\\nrecomputes byte masks, alignment, and shift selection from `alu_result`\\non every access. Hoisting that address-lane work earlier should shorten\\nthe hot memory path and reduce fanout without changing architectural\\nbehavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Extend the EX/MEM bundle with precomputed memory-lane metadata such as\\nthe aligned address, byte mask, shift amount, and misalign flag, then\\nhave `ex_stage.sv` derive those fields once from `alu_result` and\\n`mem_width` before `mem_stage.sv` consumes them directly. This keeps the\\nRVFI, trap, and retirement contract unchanged while trimming redundant\\nwidth-based logic from the memory-access critical path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the EX/MEM bundle with precomputed memory-lane metadata for address alignment, byte masking, and shift control.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive and latch the memory-lane metadata once from the ALU result and load/store width before the MEM stage.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the precomputed lane metadata so the memory stage no longer repeats width-based mask, alignment, and shift logic.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the EX/MEM bundle with precomputed memory-lane metadata for address alignment, byte masking, and shift control.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive and latch the memory-lane metadata once from the ALU result and load/store width before the MEM stage.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the precomputed lane metadata so the memory stage no longer repeats width-based mask, alignment, and shift logic.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 342.69, \"delta_pct\": 6.12, \"vs_baseline\": 21.17, \"fmax_mhz\": 153.92, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10369, \"ff\": 1959, \"seeds\": [153.92, 157.01, 137.57], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-16T09:48:46.395703Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-002-r8s1 (improvement, +6.12%): Hoisting load/store lane decode into EX helps when MEM can consume aligned address, byte mask, shift, and misalign metadata directly, because it removes width-based recomputation from the hot memory path without changing RVFI or trap semantics.\"}\n25-{\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r8s2\", \"title\": \"Return-only stack predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark still pays a repeatable bubble on function returns, and the prior\\nbroader predictor attempts were too expensive in IF. A very small return\\nstack can target that hot path without adding full BTB logic or changing\\nthe architectural redirect source of truth.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark still pays a repeatable bubble on function returns, and the prior\\nbroader predictor attempts were too expensive in IF. A very small return\\nstack can target that hot path without adding full BTB logic or changing\\nthe architectural redirect source of truth.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny return-address stack that predicts only canonical JALR returns.\\nUpdate it from already-latched PC+4 on resolved calls, use it speculatively\\nonly when the fetched instruction decodes as a return, and keep EX-stage\\nredirection authoritative for recovery. By narrowing the predictor to\\nreturns only, the design should stay much cheaper than the earlier\\ncall/return predictor while still removing recurring control-flow bubbles.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the return-stack hint for speculative next-PC selection on canonical returns, but always yield to EX-stage redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire resolved call/return metadata and PC+4 into the predictor update path without changing RVFI or trap behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/return_stack.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny return-address stack and canonical return-classification logic.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the return-stack hint for speculative next-PC selection on canonical returns, but always yield to EX-stage redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire resolved call/return metadata and PC+4 into the predictor update path without changing RVFI or trap behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/return_stack.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny return-address stack and canonical return-classification logic.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: pc_fwd_ch0\\nsn_bgeu_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\\nSBY  6:16:21 [insn_bgeu_ch0] summary: Elapsed