", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-003-r8s2 (broken, n/a): A tiny return stack only helps if its speculative fetch-side target stays synchronized with the architectural pipeline; otherwise canonical JALR return hints can desynchronize `pc_fwd` even when the predictor is return-only.\"}\n26-{\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r9s0\", \"title\": \"Source-read stall masks\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock still compares both source register fields for every\\ninstruction, even when the opcode class does not architecturally read one\\nor both sources. That creates avoidable compare fanout and can inject false\\nbubbles on common immediate and U-type instructions in CoreMark.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock still compares both source register fields for every\\ninstruction, even when the opcode class does not architecturally read one\\nor both sources. That creates avoidable compare fanout and can inject false\\nbubbles on common immediate and U-type instructions in CoreMark.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add exact `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` bits to the IF-stage predecode bundle,\\nthen gate `hazard_unit.sv`'s load-use compare logic with those bits so it\\nonly checks source registers that the current instruction actually reads.\\nThis should remove false stalls on OP-IMM, LOAD, JALR, LUI, AUIPC, JAL,\\nFENCE, and SYSTEM forms while slightly shrinking the hot hazard path, all\\nwithout changing RVFI, traps, or retirement order.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add source-read flags to the predecode bundle so later stages can distinguish architecturally used vs unused rs fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch exact `uses_rs1` / `uses_rs2` bits alongside the existing predecode metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate the load-use compare tree with the source-read flags so unused rs fields cannot trigger false stalls.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add source-read flags to the predecode bundle so later stages can distinguish architecturally used vs unused rs fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch exact `uses_rs1` / `uses_rs2` bits alongside the existing predecode metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate the load-use compare tree with the source-read flags so unused rs fields cannot trigger false stalls.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"cosim_failed: selftest.elf\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 9, \"scribe_skipped\": \"PermissionError: scribe touched off-limits paths and was rolled back: ['cores/bench/test/test_decoder.py']\"}\n27-{\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r9s1\", \"title\": \"One-hot decode classes\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The hot decode path still rebuilds opcode/funct legality and instruction\\nclass information from the raw 32-bit instruction in ID. Hoisting that\\nclassification into fetch-time predecode should cut repeated case-tree\\nwork and narrow the control fanout seen by the rest of the pipe.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The hot decode path still rebuilds opcode/funct legality and instruction\\nclass information from the raw 32-bit instruction in ID. Hoisting that\\nclassification into fetch-time predecode should cut repeated case-tree\\nwork and narrow the control fanout seen by the rest of the pipe.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add compact one-hot instruction-class metadata to the IF-stage predecode\\nbundle, then have ID consume those cached classes when forming control and\\nhazard inputs instead of repeatedly re-decoding the same opcode/funct\\npatterns from `instr[31:0]`. Keep the decoder's legality rules unchanged,\\nbut make the common control path structurally narrower so EX and MEM see\\nless combinational decode work on every cycle.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the predecode and pipeline bundles with compact one-hot instruction-class metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch the instruction-class metadata once at fetch time.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the predecoded classes when building control signals instead of re-decoding from the full instruction word.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep legality semantics identical while simplifying dispatch around the predecoded instruction class inputs.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the predecode and pipeline bundles with compact one-hot instruction-class metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch the instruction-class metadata once at fetch time.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the predecoded classes when building control signals instead of re-decoding from the full instruction word.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep legality semantics identical while simplifying dispatch around the predecoded instruction class inputs.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 316.84, \"delta_pct\": -7.54, \"vs_baseline\": 12.03, \"fmax_mhz\": 142.31, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9745, \"ff\": 1958, \"seeds\": [154.56, 142.31, 137.99], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-16T11:09:48.200417Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-002-r9s1 (regression, -7.54%): Hoisting one-hot instruction classes only pays when it removes enough work from the hot decode path; if ID still rechecks `funct3`/`funct7` and the wider predecode bundle adds fanout, the extra metadata can slow CoreMark instead of helping.\"}\n28-{\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r9s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny bimodal branch predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends a meaningful fraction of its time on the same\\nconditional backedges and short control-flow loops. The earlier static\\nand stack-based predictor ideas were either too expensive or too broad,\\nso a smaller learned direction predictor is the best remaining angle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends a meaningful fraction of its time on the same\\nconditional backedges and short control-flow loops. The earlier static\\nand stack-based predictor ideas were either too expensive or too broad,\\nso a smaller learned direction predictor is the best remaining angle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny direct-mapped bimodal predictor that stores only 2-bit taken\\nconfidence for conditional branches, with the existing IF-stage immediate\\ndecode used to choose between fall-through and the predicted branch target.\\nUpdate the table only from retired conditional branches, keep EX-stage\\nresolution authoritative for recovery, and avoid BTB or return-stack\\ntarget storage entirely so the predictor stays cheap enough for this FPGA.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use a small bimodal direction predictor to speculatively choose fall-through vs the decoded branch target before EX resolves the branch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire retired conditional-branch outcome information into the predictor update path without changing the RVFI or trap contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny direct-mapped 2-bit branch-direction table with conservative fall-through defaults and retirement-time updates.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use a small bimodal direction predictor to speculatively choose fall-through vs the decoded branch target before EX resolves the branch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire retired conditional-branch outcome information into the predictor update path without changing the RVFI or trap contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny direct-mapped 2-bit branch-direction table with conservative fall-through defaults and retirement-time updates.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: insn_beq_ch0\\nnsn_bltu_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY  7:51:06 [insn_bltu_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_insn_check_sv_198_154 at rvfi_insn_check.sv:198.6-198.31 step 20\\nSBY  7:51:06 [insn_bltu_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\nSBY  7:53:59 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:10:10  waiting for solver (10 minutes)\\nSBY  7:56:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:12:50  Status: passed\\nSBY  7:56:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=0)\\nSBY  7:56:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\\nSBY  7:56:39 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:12:55 (775)\\nSBY  7:56:39 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:02:22 (142)\\nSBY  7:56:39 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\\nSBY  7:56:39 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\\nSBY  7:56:39 [reg_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\\n\\nFormal: 46 passed, 7 failed\\nFailed: insn_beq_ch0 insn_bge_ch0 insn_bgeu_ch0 insn_blt_ch0 insn_bltu_ch0 insn_bne_ch0 pc_fwd_ch0\\n