{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778933706120,"sessionID":"ses_1cf4ad38fffet6KoTg5NSa2pJh","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_aoGmSyb71fPJhnHssR346naA","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r11s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-003-r11s2\n+title: \"Retired loop-backedge predictor\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark still burns cycles on the same hot loop backedges, but the\n+  broader predictor attempts paid too much in IF logic or speculative\n+  state. A tiny predictor anchored to retired control-flow state is the\n+  narrowest remaining way to hide those fetch bubbles without changing\n+  the architectural redirect contract.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a single-entry loop-backedge predictor that remembers the most\n+  recent retired taken conditional branch PC and target, then speculates\n+  only on exact PC hits for backward branches. Train it strictly from\n+  retired branch outcomes, keep EX-stage redirect authoritative for every\n+  recovery path, and avoid any extra speculative training state so the\n+  predictor stays small enough to help CoreMark without dragging Fmax.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consume a tiny loop-backedge hint for speculative next-PC selection, but always yield to EX-stage redirect recovery.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire retired conditional-branch outcome information into the predictor update path without changing RVFI or trap behavior.\"\n+  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n+    description: \"Add a single-entry loop-backedge predictor with exact-PC tagging, a cached target, and conservative fall-through on miss.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r11s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/a