{"type":"text","timestamp":1778902647527,"sessionID":"ses_1d12497a9ffe568uAi8wF8Dikt","part":{"id":"prt_e2edc42c0001K8cEkQcHxibOM2","messageID":"msg_e2edc1472001Y6W5LMFcSuKlIY","sessionID":"ses_1d12497a9ffe568uAi8wF8Dikt","type":"text","text":"I’m writing the hypothesis file now. The shape is intentionally small: one predictor module, IF lookup, and a simple update path from resolved branches.","time":{"start":1778902647488,"end":1778902647526},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0c646628745729e4016a07e6775c748199999dd7e73f6ca724","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778902648342,"sessionID":"ses_1d12497a9ffe568uAi8wF8Dikt","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_h3nUxWNFrOMrjJlE5FXs4ocR","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r5s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-003-r5s2\n+title: \"Tiny branch-direction predictor\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark still spends cycles waiting on repeated control transfers, especially\n+  short loop backedges and recurring direct jumps. A very small predictor that\n+  learns branch direction without general BTB state could hide those bubbles\n+  while keeping the existing EX redirect path as the architectural source of\n+  truth.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a tiny direct-mapped direction predictor in IF that speculatively chooses\n+  between fall-through and the already-available control-flow target, while EX\n+  resolution remains authoritative for recovery. Keep the state to a few\n+  learned taken/not-taken bits so repeated CoreMark branches can settle quickly\n+  without the formal and timing cost of a full BTB or return-stack design.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Use predictor output to select the speculative next PC before EX resolution, but keep EX redirects as the final authority.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire resolved branch outcome information into the predictor update path without changing RVFI or trap behavior.\"\n+  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n+    description: \"Add a tiny direct-mapped branch-direction table with simple update logic and a conservative fallback to fall-through.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r5s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-re