{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778907801118,"sessionID":"ses_1d0d5ce2fffedaU5e0WLaW0zR4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_1RelNFRUxjsT4V3AGjb669en","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r6s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-003-r6s2\n+title: \"Advisory loop-backedge predictor\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark still spends cycles on repeated loop backedges and direct jumps,\n+  so the core keeps paying the EX-stage fetch bubble on control transfers\n+  that are cheap to predict statically. A predictor with no training state\n+  is the lowest-risk way to hide more of that control-flow latency.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a purely combinational BTFNT-style hint in IF: predict direct JALs\n+  taken and predict conditional branches taken only when the immediate is\n+  backward, while forward branches fall through. Keep EX-stage resolution\n+  as the architectural source of truth for redirects and mispredict repair,\n+  so the predictor only changes speculative fetch and not RVFI behavior.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add a stateless static branch-direction hint in fetch, but leave EX redirects and wrong-path squashing authoritative.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r6s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r6s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r6s2.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experimen