{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778912333152,"sessionID":"ses_1d0910de0ffeXbZ55rv1eHOUXW","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_HM131uSAUqCQKNCwQy1I0tEl","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r7s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-003-r7s2\n+title: \"Single-entry loop predictor\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark has hot loop backedges that repeat many times, but the prior\n+  broader predictors paid too much cost in IF logic and formal complexity.\n+  A one-entry loop cache should capture the dominant repeat without the\n+  training and state overhead of a general BTB or return stack.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a single-entry loop predictor in IF that remembers the last taken\n+  conditional backedge's PC and target, and speculatively redirects only on\n+  a tag hit. Train it only from resolved EX outcomes, keep EX redirect\n+  authoritative on every miss or mismatch, and avoid speculative training\n+  state beyond that one cached loop target.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consume a tiny loop-predictor hint for speculative next-PC selection, but always yield to EX-stage redirect recovery.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire resolved branch outcomes into the predictor update path without changing the RVFI or trap contract.\"\n+  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n+    description: \"Add a single-entry tagged loop-target cache with conservative fall-through on miss and update-on-resolved-branch behavior.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r7s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r7s2.yaml\n=====================================