{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778919309405,"sessionID":"ses_1d0264583ffe1bCdEqro7y3me0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_xn6wnOkkli83vc9cQqWPwZhX","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r8s1.yaml","offset":1,"limit":120},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r8s1.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260516-002-r8s1\n2: title: \"Move memory lane work earlier\"\n3: category: structural\n4: motivation: |\n5:   CoreMark is still heavy on loads and stores, and the current MEM stage\n6:   recomputes byte masks, alignment, and shift selection from `alu_result`\n7:   on every access. Hoisting that address-lane work earlier should shorten\n8:   the hot memory path and reduce fanout without changing architectural\n9:   behavior.\n10: hypothesis: |\n11:   Extend the EX/MEM bundle with precomputed memory-lane metadata such as\n12:   the aligned address, byte mask, shift amount, and misalign flag, then\n13:   have `ex_stage.sv` derive those fields once from `alu_result` and\n14:   `mem_width` before `mem_stage.sv` consumes them directly. This keeps the\n15:   RVFI, trap, and retirement contract unchanged while trimming redundant\n16:   width-based logic from the memory-access critical path.\n17: expected_impact:\n18:   fitness_delta_pct: 4\n19:   confidence: medium\n20: changes:\n21:   - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n22:     description: \"Extend the EX/MEM bundle with precomputed memory-lane metadata for address alignment, byte masking, and shift control.\"\n23:   - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n24:     description: \"Derive and latch the memory-lane metadata once from the ALU result and load/store width before the MEM stage.\"\n25:   - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n26:     description: \"Consume the precomputed lane metadata so the memory stage no longer repeats width-based mask, alignment, and shift logic.\"\n\n(End of file - total 26 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260516-002-r8s1\ntitle: \"Move memory lane work earlier\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  CoreMark is still heavy on loads and stores, and the current MEM stage\n  recomputes byte masks, alignment, and shift selection from `alu_result`\n  on every access. Hoisting that address-lane work earlier should shorten\n  the hot memory path and reduce fanout without changing architectural\n  behavior.\nhypothesis: |\n  Extend the EX/MEM bundle with precomputed memory-lane metadata such as\n  the aligned address, byte mask, shift amount, and misalign flag, then\n  have `ex_stage.sv` derive those fields once from `alu_result` and\n  `mem_width` before `mem_stage.sv` consumes them directly. This keeps the\n  RVFI, trap, and retirement contract unchanged while trimming redundant\n  width-based logic from the memory-access critical path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r8s1.yaml","time":{"start":1778919309033,"end":1778919309403}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0635a8af439e60f4016a08278ccb748199a6ffb39ec004a2ec"}},"id":"prt_e2fda7ed0001f44IJKkjZ31nJ4","sessionID":"ses_1d0264583ffe1bCdEqro7y3me0","messageID":"msg_e2fda6d5c001WQzkt1MnCMetWd"}}
