{"type":"text","timestamp":1778990026131,"sessionID":"ses_1cbef4315ffe5Zcadj3gdPxx4U","part":{"id":"prt_e34118d6f001luwMwz06qU7Gcn","messageID":"msg_e341149ba001dx4I4Jnt73d3Rl","sessionID":"ses_1cbef4315ffe5Zcadj3gdPxx4U","type":"text","text":"Writing the hypothesis now. I’m keeping it narrow: exact rs-read masks, only on the load-use interlock, so the implementation stays conservative and avoids the broader predictor-style risk.","time":{"start":1778990026096,"end":1778990026115},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0f67925847e6f8ab016a093bc9e8a081909408784cf77ccc39","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778990027597,"sessionID":"ses_1cbef4315ffe5Zcadj3gdPxx4U","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_IsAW95lacUZo6SgDduc5LF85","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r12s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r12s0\n+title: \"Exact source-read stall masks\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The load-use interlock still compares both raw source fields on every\n+  instruction, even when the opcode class does not architecturally read\n+  one of them. That adds always-on compare fanout and can also create\n+  false bubbles on common immediate and U-type instructions in CoreMark.\n+  A conservative source-read mask should trim that hot hazard path without\n+  changing retirement behavior.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add exact `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` bits to the fetch-time predecode\n+  bundle, derived from the same opcode/funct classification the decoder\n+  already trusts. Then gate the load-use compare tree in `hazard_unit.sv`\n+  with those bits so it only checks source registers the current\n+  instruction definitely reads. Keep ambiguous cases pessimistic, so any\n+  uncertain opcode still stalls rather than risking an architectural miss.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add conservative `uses_rs1` / `uses_rs2` fields to the predecode bundle so source-read intent rides with the fetched instruction.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute and latch the exact source-read masks alongside the existing opcode/funct predecode.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Use the source-read masks to skip irrelevant load-use compares and avoid false stalls on immediate-style instructions.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the predecoded source-read masks into the hazard path without changing RVFI, traps, or retirement order.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r12s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r12s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r12s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r12s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r12s0\n+title: \"Exact source-read stall masks\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The load-use interlock still compares both raw source fields on every\n+  instruction, even when the opcode class does not architecturally read\n+  one of them. That adds always-on compare fanout and can also create\n+  false bubbles on common immediate and U-type instructions in CoreMark.\n+  A conservative source-read mask should trim that hot hazard path without\n+  changing retirement behavior.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add exact `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` bits to the fetch-time predecode\n+  bundle, derived from the same opcode/funct classification the decoder\n+  already trusts. Then gate the load-use compare tree in `hazard_unit.sv`\n+  with those bits so it only checks source registers the current\n+  instruction definitely reads. Keep ambiguous cases pessimistic, so any\n+  uncertain opcode still stalls rather than risking an architectural miss.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add conservative `uses_rs1` / `uses_rs2` fields to the predecode bundle so source-read intent rides with the fetched instruction.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute and latch the exact source-read masks alongside the existing opcode/funct predecode.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Use the source-read masks to skip irrelevant load-use compares and avoid false stalls on immediate-style instructions.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the predecoded source-read masks into the hazard path without changing RVFI, traps, or retirement order.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r12s0.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r12s0.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r12s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r12s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r12s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r12s0\n+title: \"Exact source-read stall masks\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The load-use interlock still compares both raw source fields on every\n+  instruction, even when the opcode class does not architecturally read\n+  one of them. That adds always-on compare fanout and can also create\n+  false bubbles on common immediate and U-type instructions in CoreMark.\n+  A conservative source-read mask should trim that hot hazard path without\n+  changing retirement behavior.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add exact `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` bits to the fetch-time predecode\n+  bundle, derived from the same opcode/funct classification the decoder\n+  already trusts. Then gate the load-use compare tree in `hazard_unit.sv`\n+  with those bits so it only checks source registers the current\n+  instruction definitely reads. Keep ambiguous cases pessimistic, so any\n+  uncertain opcode still stalls rather than risking an architectural miss.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add conservative `uses_rs1` / `uses_rs2` fields to the predecode bundle so source-read intent rides with the fetched instruction.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute and latch the exact source-read masks alongside the existing opcode/funct predecode.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Use the source-read masks to skip irrelevant load-use compares and avoid false stalls on immediate-style instructions.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the predecoded source-read masks into the hazard path without changing RVFI, traps, or retirement order.\"\n","additions":29,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r12s0.yaml","time":{"start":1778990027471,"end":1778990027483}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0f67925847e6f8ab016a093bca038081908a445aeace277022"}},"id":"prt_e34118d88001XE0r5MbIOmb2Pg","sessionID":"ses_1cbef4315ffe5Zcadj3gdPxx4U","messageID":"msg_e341149ba001dx4I4Jnt73d3Rl"}}
