t\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the EX/MEM bundle with precomputed memory-lane metadata for address alignment, byte masking, and shift control.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive and latch the memory-lane metadata once from the ALU result and load/store width before the MEM stage.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the precomputed lane metadata so the memory stage no longer repeats width-based mask, alignment, and shift logic.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the EX/MEM bundle with precomputed memory-lane metadata for address alignment, byte masking, and shift control.\"...\n  Line 26: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r9s0\", \"title\": \"Source-read stall masks\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock still compares both source register fields for every\\ninstruction, even when the opcode class does not architecturally read one\\nor both sources. That creates avoidable compare fanout and can inject false\\nbubbles on common immediate and U-type instructions in CoreMark.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock still compares both source register fields for every\\ninstruction, even when the opcode class does not architecturally read one\\nor both sources. That creates avoidable compare fanout and can inject false\\nbubbles on common immediate and U-type instructions in CoreMark.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add exact `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` bits to the IF-stage predecode bundle,\\nthen gate `hazard_unit.sv`'s load-use compare logic with those bits so it\\nonly checks source registers that the current instruction actually reads.\\nThis should remove false stalls on OP-IMM, LOAD, JALR, LUI, AUIPC, JAL,\\nFENCE, and SYSTEM forms while slightly shrinking the hot hazard path, all\\nwithout changing RVFI, traps, or retirement order.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add source-read flags to the predecode bundle so later stages can distinguish architecturally used vs unused rs fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch exact `uses_rs1` / `uses_rs2` bits alongside the existing predecode metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate the load-use compare tree with the source-read flags so unused rs fields cannot trigger false stalls.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add source-read flags to the predecode bundle so later stages can distinguish architecturally used vs unused rs fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.s...\n  Line 27: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r9s1\", \"title\": \"One-hot decode classes\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The hot decode path still rebuilds opcode/funct legality and instruction\\nclass information from the raw 32-bit instruction in ID. Hoisting that\\nclassification into fetch-time predecode should cut repeated case-tree\\nwork and narrow the control fanout seen by the rest of the pipe.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The hot decode path still rebuilds opcode/funct legality and instruction\\nclass information from the raw 32-bit instruction in ID. Hoisting that\\nclassification into fetch-time predecode should cut repeated case-tree\\nwork and narrow the control fanout seen by the rest of the pipe.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add compact one-hot instruction-class metadata to the IF-stage predecode\\nbundle, then have ID consume those cached classes when forming control and\\nhazard inputs instead of repeatedly re-decoding the same opcode/funct\\npatterns from `instr[31:0]`. Keep the decoder's legality rules unchanged,\\nbut make the common control path structurally narrower so EX and MEM see\\nless combinational decode work on every cycle.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the predecode and pipeline bundles with compact one-hot instruction-class metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch the instruction-class metadata once at fetch time.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the predecoded classes when building control signals instead of re-decoding from the full instruction word.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep legality semantics identical while simplifying dispatch around the predecoded instruction class inputs.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the predecode and pipeline bundles with compact one-hot instructi...\n  Line 29: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r10s0\", \"title\": \"Decoder-aligned stall masks\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on instructions that do not read both\\nsource registers. The current load-use interlock still compares raw rs\\nfields unconditionally, so it burns fanout and can inject false bubbles\\non common immediate and U-type instructions.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on instructions that do not read both\\nsource registers. The current load-use interlock still compares raw rs\\nfields unconditionally, so it burns fanout and can inject false bubbles\\non common immediate and U-type instructions.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add exact `uses_rs1` / `uses_rs2` metadata to the fetch-time predecode\\nbundle, derived from the same opcode-class rules the decoder uses, and\\nuse those bits to gate the load-use compare tree in `hazard_unit.sv`.\\nThis should remove avoidable stall checks on instructions that do not\\narchitecturally read rs2, while keeping RVFI, traps, and forwarding\\nbehavior unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` to the predecode bundle so source-read intent can ride with the fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch exact source-operand-use bits alongside the existing predecode fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate the load-use compare logic with the source-read bits so unused rs fields cannot trigger false stalls.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` to the predecode bundle so source-read intent can ride with the fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch exact source-operand-use bits alongside the existing predecode fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard...\n  Line 30: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r10s1\", \"title\": \"Split retire and writeback\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current MEM/WB boundary carries a lot of RVFI-only state through the\\nsame bundle that feeds the regfile and forwarding logic. That makes the\\nhottest post-MEM path wider than it needs to be.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current MEM/WB boundary carries a lot of RVFI-only state through the\\nsame bundle that feeds the regfile and forwarding logic. That makes the\\nhottest post-MEM path wider than it needs to be.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split the wide retirement snapshot from the narrow writeback/bypass path:\\nkeep only rd, rd_wdata, reg_write, and valid on the signals used by the\\nregfile and forwarding network, and carry the full RVFI snapshot on a\\nseparate sideband bundle. This should reduce fanout and routing pressure on\\nthe MEM/WB boundary without changing architectural retirement behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define separate narrow writeback and full retire-snapshot bundle types so the post-MEM path can be split cleanly.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the narrow writeback data separately from the full RVFI retirement snapshot.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the narrow writeback metadata instead of the full MEM/WB bundle for bypass comparisons.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/wb_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drive the regfile from the narrow writeback bundle with no dependency on RVFI-only fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the split bundles so RVFI comes from the retire snapshot while writeback and forwarding use the narrow path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define separate narrow writeback and full retire-snapshot bundle types so the post-MEM path can be split cleanly.\"}, {\"file\": \"r...\n  Line 31: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r10s2\", \"title\": \"Narrow loop-backedge predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends a lot of time on the same loop backedges, but the\\nbroader predictor attempts so far have paid too much in IF logic, state,\\nor formal complexity. A very small predictor that only tracks the most\\nrecent conditional backedge should be cheaper than a BTB or return stack\\nwhile still removing a common fetch bubble.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends a lot of time on the same loop backedges, but the\\nbroader predictor attempts so far have paid too much in IF logic, state,\\nor formal complexity. A very small predictor that only tracks the most\\nrecent conditional backedge should be cheaper than a BTB or return stack\\nwhile still removing a common fetch bubble.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny one-entry loop-backedge predictor in IF that remembers the last\\ntaken conditional branch PC, its target, and a single taken bit. Speculate\\nonly on exact PC hits for backward conditional branches, update only from\\nretired conditional branches, and keep EX-stage redirect authoritative for\\nrecovery. This narrows the predictor enough to avoid the fanout and control\\ncomplexity that hurt earlier predictor ideas while still targeting CoreMark's\\ndominant loop pattern.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the loop-backedge hint to choose the speculative next PC on exact-hit backward branches, but always yield to EX-stage redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire retired conditional-branch outcome information into the predictor update path without changing the RVFI or trap contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a single-entry loop-backedge predictor with one-bit taken state, exact PC tagging, and conservative fall-through on miss.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"conf...\n  Line 32: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r11s0\", \"title\": \"Cache pc+4 in IF\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The sequential fall-through PC is needed on every instruction, but the\\ncurrent core still recomputes `pc + 4` in ID. Hoisting that universal add\\ninto fetch should trim a small amount of always-on decode-path logic and\\nreduce fanout through the hot IF/ID -> ID/EX boundary.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The sequential fall-through PC is needed on every instruction, but the\\ncurrent core still recomputes `pc + 4` in ID. Hoisting that universal add\\ninto fetch should trim a small amount of always-on decode-path logic and\\nreduce fanout through the hot IF/ID -> ID/EX boundary.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a cached `pc_plus4` field to the IF/ID bundle, compute it once in\\n`if_stage.sv`, and have `id_stage.sv` latch that value directly instead of\\nrebuilding `pc + 4` every cycle. This keeps retirement, traps, and RVFI\\nbehavior unchanged while moving a universal 32-bit add out of the ID hot\\npath.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add `pc_plus4` to the IF/ID bundle so fetch can carry the sequential PC forward.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch `pc_plus4` alongside the fetched instruction metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the cached sequential PC instead of recomputing `pc + 4` in decode.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add `pc_plus4` to the IF/ID bundle so fetch can carry the sequential PC forward.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch `pc_plus4` alongside the fetched instruction metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the cached sequential PC instead of recomputing `pc + 4` in decode.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 310.99, \"delta_pct\": -9.25, \"vs_baseline\": 9.9...\n  Line 33: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r11s1\", \"title\": \"Hoist JALR target\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The remaining hot control-flow work in EX is the JALR rs1+imm add and\\nits misalignment bookkeeping. CoreMark still exercises call/return paths\\nenough that moving that arithmetic earlier should trim the execute-side\\ntiming cone without changing the architectural redirect contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The remaining hot control-flow work in EX is the JALR rs1+imm add and\\nits misalignment bookkeeping. CoreMark still exercises call/return paths\\nenough that moving that arithmetic earlier should trim the execute-side\\ntiming cone without changing the architectural redirect contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a narrow ID-side JALR precompute path: forward the rs1 operand into\\ndecode only for JALR, latch the resulting `jalr_target` in the ID/EX\\nbundle, and have EX reuse that stored target for redirect and\\nmisalignment checks. Keep EX as the architectural resolve point, but\\nremove the live `rs1 + imm` adder from the critical execute path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the ID/EX bundle with a latched `jalr_target` field for JALR redirects.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose a minimal JALR-specific rs1 forwarding path that decode can use to compute the target early.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch the JALR target during decode using the forwarded rs1 operand.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the latched JALR target instead of rebuilding `rs1 + imm` in EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the new ID-side JALR target precompute path through the top-level pipeline.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the ID/EX bundle with a latched `jalr_target` field for JALR redi...\n  Line 35: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-001-r12s0\", \"title\": \"Exact source-read stall masks\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock still compares both raw source fields on every\\ninstruction, even when the opcode class does not architecturally read\\none of them. That adds always-on compare fanout and can also create\\nfalse bubbles on common immediate and U-type instructions in CoreMark.\\nA conservative source-read mask should trim that hot hazard path without\\nchanging retirement behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock still compares both raw source fields on every\\ninstruction, even when the opcode class does not architecturally read\\none of them. That adds always-on compare fanout and can also create\\nfalse bubbles on common immediate and U-type instructions in CoreMark.\\nA conservative source-read mask should trim that hot hazard path without\\nchanging retirement behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add exact `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` bits to the fetch-time predecode\\nbundle, derived from the same opcode/funct classification the decoder\\nalready trusts. Then gate the load-use compare tree in `hazard_unit.sv`\\nwith those bits so it only checks source registers the current\\ninstruction definitely reads. Keep ambiguous cases pessimistic, so any\\nuncertain opcode still stalls rather than risking an architectural miss.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add conservative `uses_rs1` / `uses_rs2` fields to the predecode bundle so source-read intent rides with the fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch the exact source-read masks alongside the existing opcode/funct predecode.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the source-read masks to skip irrelevant load-use compares and avoid false stalls on immediate-style instructions.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the predecoded sour...\n  Line 36: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-002-r12s1\", \"title\": \"Hoist full decode into fetch\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"ID still rebuilds the validated control bundle from the raw instruction on every cycle.\\nSince fetch already owns the instruction slice, hoisting decode one stage earlier should\\nshorten the hot IF/ID -> ID/EX path and reduce instruction fanout without changing\\nretirement, trap, or RVFI behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"ID still rebuilds the validated control bundle from the raw instruction on every cycle.\\nSince fetch already owns the instruction slice, hoisting decode one stage earlier should\\nshorten the hot IF/ID -> ID/EX path and reduce instruction fanout without changing\\nretirement, trap, or RVFI behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Extend the IF/ID bundle with a fully decoded control record, instantiate the existing\\ndecoder at fetch time, and latch that control alongside the predecoded instruction\\nmetadata. Then make ID a narrower register-read stage that consumes the latched control\\nbundle instead of rebuilding opcode/funct legality and control signals locally. This keeps\\nthe ISA contract identical while removing the decoder case tree from the ID critical path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the IF/ID bundle with a latched control record so fetch can hand decode results forward with the instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode each fetched instruction once at fetch time and carry the validated control bundle forward with the predecoded metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the latched control bundle and remove the local decoder/control-tree work from the hot ID path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the IF/ID bundle with a latched control record so fetch can hand decode results fo...","metadata":{"matches":27,"truncated":false},"title":"micro_opt|forward_unit|id_stage|predecoded|fanout|mux|stall","time":{"start":1778990626063,"end":1778990626071}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_095afaaeb89592b6016a093e21f42481938256bed0074b8039"}},"id":"prt_e341ab50d002UM4NSOjoo3RV2r","sessionID":"ses_1cbe55bfcffesz8Hsgcy3MH9Wb","messageID":"msg_e341aa449001CiSl4pLUBgorox"}}
