{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778990692752,"sessionID":"ses_1cbe55bfcffesz8Hsgcy3MH9Wb","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_zXZ1siheLTnNvUcMjLf01ddD","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r13s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r13s0\n+title: Source-read compare gating\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The load-use interlock still compares both source fields on every instruction,\n+  even when the opcode never reads rs2. That burns always-on compare fanout and\n+  can inject false bubbles on common immediate-style CoreMark instructions.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add exact `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` masks to the fetch-time predecode bundle,\n+  derive them from the already-validated opcode class, and use them to gate the\n+  load-use compare tree in `hazard_unit.sv`. Keep illegal or ambiguous cases\n+  pessimistic so the interlock only disappears when a source operand is definitely\n+  unused.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Extend the predecode bundle with exact source-read masks for rs1 and rs2.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute and latch the source-read masks alongside the existing fetch-time predecode.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the new predecode masks into the hazard unit inputs.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate the load-use compare tree with the source-read masks so unused source fields cannot trigger false stalls.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r13s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-