{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778990696307,"sessionID":"ses_1cbe55bfcffesz8Hsgcy3MH9Wb","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_8wVWjRvyyd3Vc3O3JWLbiFH6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r13s0.yaml","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r13s0.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260517-001-r13s0\n2: title: Source-read compare gating\n3: category: micro_opt\n4: motivation: |\n5:   The load-use interlock still compares both source fields on every instruction,\n6:   even when the opcode never reads rs2. That burns always-on compare fanout and\n7:   can inject false bubbles on common immediate-style CoreMark instructions.\n8: hypothesis: |\n9:   Add exact `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` masks to the fetch-time predecode bundle,\n10:   derive them from the already-validated opcode class, and use them to gate the\n11:   load-use compare tree in `hazard_unit.sv`. Keep illegal or ambiguous cases\n12:   pessimistic so the interlock only disappears when a source operand is definitely\n13:   unused.\n14: expected_impact:\n15:   fitness_delta_pct: 5\n16:   confidence: medium\n17: changes:\n18:   - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n19:     description: \"Extend the predecode bundle with exact source-read masks for rs1 and rs2.\"\n20:   - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n21:     description: \"Compute and latch the source-read masks alongside the existing fetch-time predecode.\"\n22:   - file: rtl/core.sv\n23:     description: \"Wire the new predecode masks into the hazard unit inputs.\"\n24:   - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n25:     description: \"Gate the load-use compare tree with the source-read masks so unused source fields cannot trigger false stalls.\"\n\n(End of file - total 25 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260517-001-r13s0\ntitle: Source-read compare gating\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The load-use interlock still compares both source fields on every instruction,\n  even when the opcode never reads rs2. That burns always-on compare fanout and\n  can inject false bubbles on common immediate-style CoreMark instructions.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add exact `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` masks to the fetch-time predecode bundle,\n  derive them from the already-validated opcode class, and use them to gate the\n  load-use compare tree in `hazard_unit.sv`. Keep illegal or ambiguous cases\n  pessimistic so the interlock only disappears when a source operand is definitely\n  unused.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Extend the predecode bundle with exact source-read masks for rs1 and rs2.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r13s0.yaml","time":{"start":1778990696287,"end":1778990696306}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0bca3686775a624a016a093e6800a88190ac579c5b815e8226"}},"id":"prt_e341bc69c00119adJFOEiFE2vi","sessionID":"ses_1cbe55bfcffesz8Hsgcy3MH9Wb","messageID":"msg_e341bba87001ev99qW0gEz9NgM"}}
