rk/MHz without changing retirement or RVFI behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time in short loops, so the current EX-resolved\\nbranch path still pays avoidable fetch bubbles on repeated taken branches.\\nA predictor that redirects IF earlier, but keeps EX as the source of truth,\\ncan improve CoreMark/MHz without changing retirement or RVFI behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the failed stateful BTB idea with a fully combinational static\\npredictor in IF: predict backward conditional branches taken, forward\\nconditional branches not taken, and always predict JALs taken from the\\nfetched instruction. This keeps the predictor update path trivial, avoids\\nspeculative training state, and should hide more of the branch penalty on\\nCoreMark's hot loops while preserving the existing mispredict redirect.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use a static predictor to choose the speculative next PC before EX resolution.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small combinational BTFNT predictor that decodes the fetched instruction and emits the predicted next PC.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use a static predictor to choose the speculative next PC before EX resolution.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small combinational BTFNT predictor that decodes the fetched instruction and emits the predicted next PC.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_...\n  Line 8: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r3s0\", \"title\": \"Reuse latched JAL targets\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The core already latches `pc + imm` in ID for branch targets, but EX still\\nrecomputes the same add for JALs before redirecting fe