{"type":"text","timestamp":1778991391409,"sessionID":"ses_1cbdaa83fffe41UT9hhrGrxSD3","part":{"id":"prt_e342661fe001t4g8HuiOZWIj9M","messageID":"msg_e3425e9a0001up7SxSGfBvOSDd","sessionID":"ses_1cbdaa83fffe41UT9hhrGrxSD3","type":"text","text":"The hypothesis is now narrowed to conservative source-read masks that prune both hazard and forwarding compares. I’m adding the YAML file in the bench hypotheses folder with the exact required ID.","time":{"start":1778991391230,"end":1778991391408},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_04b9a3f58c53a15c016a09411f199c8190b79d22e0fb22edeb","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778991393522,"sessionID":"ses_1cbdaa83fffe41UT9hhrGrxSD3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_dmE1tLMeCxAgVLod8DXiTGSF","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r14s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r14s0\n+title: \"Operand-read compare pruning\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark mixes many immediate and single-source instructions with a small\n+  number of true register-register dependencies. The current load-use and\n+  forwarding compares still look at both source fields on every cycle, which\n+  adds always-on fanout and can create false stalls on instructions that do\n+  not architecturally read rs2.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add exact `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` bits to the fetch-time control bundle,\n+  derived from the same validated opcode/funct classification the decoder\n+  already uses, and route those bits into both the load-use interlock and the\n+  EX-stage forwarding compares. This should prune irrelevant compare logic\n+  for instructions that do not read a source register while keeping all\n+  ambiguous cases pessimistic so RVFI, traps, and retirement order stay the\n+  same.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Extend the control/predecode bundles with conservative `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` metadata.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Populate the source-read metadata from the validated opcode/funct classification without changing legality rules.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch the source-read metadata with the fetched instruction so downstream logic can use it without re-decoding.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate the load-use compare tree with the source-read metadata so unused source fields cannot trigger false stalls.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Use the source-read metadata to prune unnecessary EX/MEM and MEM/WB source comparisons.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the new source-read metadata from fetch into hazard and forwarding without changing the RVFI contract.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r14s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r14s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r14s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r14s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r14s0\n+title: \"Operand-read compare pruning\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark mixes many immediate and single-source instructions with a small\n+  number of true register-register dependencies. The current load-use and\n+  forwarding compares still look at both source fields on every cycle, which\n+  adds always-on fanout and can create false stalls on instructions that do\n+  not architecturally read rs2.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add exact `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` bits to the fetch-time control bundle,\n+  derived from the same validated opcode/funct classification the decoder\n+  already uses, and route those bits into both the load-use interlock and the\n+  EX-stage forwarding compares. This should prune irrelevant compare logic\n+  for instructions that do not read a source register while keeping all\n+  ambiguous cases pessimistic so RVFI, traps, and retirement order stay the\n+  same.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: r