p target for JAL even though the\\nsame PC+imm value is already available from ID. Reusing that latched\\ntarget should trim another 32-bit adder from the execute-side timing\\npath without changing retirement, trap, or RVFI behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"EX still rebuilds the PC-relative jump target for JAL even though the\\nsame PC+imm value is already available from ID. Reusing that latched\\ntarget should trim another 32-bit adder from the execute-side timing\\npath without changing retirement, trap, or RVFI behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Use the precomputed ID-stage branch target for JAL redirects and\\nmisalignment checks, and leave EX to compute only the rs1+imm target\\nneeded for JALR. This keeps control flow identical while removing one\\nmore hot add/mux pair from the EX critical path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Reuse the latched PC-relative target for JAL so EX only computes the JALR target and associated trap/redirect bookkeeping.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Reuse the latched PC-relative target for JAL so EX only computes the JALR target and associated trap/redirect bookkeeping.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 310.65, \"delta_pct\": -0.38, \"vs_baseline\": 9.84, \"fmax_mhz\": 139.53, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10058, \"ff\": 1923, \"seeds\": [139.53, 141.16, 135.67], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-16T02:02:22.027157Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 3}\n\n  Line 11: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r4s0\", \"title\": \"Latch writeback data in MEM\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"WB still rebuilds the final rd_wdata with a small mem_