{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778992263963,"sessionID":"ses_1cbccf440ffesSExN0HGL84oGD","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_aJNQDDxkY46du8ZeWHnJW4XN","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-003-r15s2.yaml","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-003-r15s2.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260517-003-r15s2\n2: title: Retired loop-count predictor\n3: category: predictor\n4: motivation: |\n5:   CoreMark keeps revisiting the same short backward loops, so the core still\n6:   pays the EX-stage branch bubble on a very regular control-flow pattern.\n7:   A predictor that learns only from retired loop branches is narrower than a\n8:   general BTB and should be much safer than the earlier fetch-side stateful\n9:   attempts.\n10: hypothesis: |\n11:   Add a single-entry retired loop-count predictor that tracks the most recent\n12:   backward conditional branch PC, its target, and a small confidence counter.\n13:   Speculate only on exact-PC hits for that loop, train only from retired branch\n14:   outcomes, and keep EX-stage redirect authoritative for recovery so the\n15:   predictor stays narrow, local, and CoreMark-focused.\n16: expected_impact:\n17:   fitness_delta_pct: 5\n18:   confidence: medium\n19: changes:\n20:   - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n21:     description: \"Use the loop predictor to choose the speculative next PC on exact-hit backward branches while preserving EX-stage redirect priority.\"\n22:   - file: rtl/core.sv\n23:     description: \"Wire retired branch PC, target, and taken/not-taken outcome into the predictor update path without changing RVFI behavior.\"\n24:   - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n25:     description: \"Add a one-entry loop-count predictor with exact-PC tagging, cached target, and conservative fall-through on miss.\"\n\n(End of file - total 25 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260517-003-r15s2\ntitle: Retired loop-count predictor\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  CoreMark keeps revisiting the same short backward loops, so the core still\n  pays the EX-stage branch bubble on a very regular control-flow pattern.\n  A predictor that learns only from retired loop branches is narrower than a\n  general BTB and should be much safer than the earlier fetch-side stateful\n  attempts.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a single-entry retired loop-count predictor that tracks the most recent\n  backward conditional branch PC, its target, and a small confidence counter.\n  Speculate only on exact-PC hits for that loop, train only from retired branch\n  outcomes, and keep EX-stage redirect authoritative for recovery so the\n  predictor stays narrow, local, and CoreMark-focused.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-003-r15s2.yaml","time":{"start":1778992263955,"end":1778992263962}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_03254b9b6fd47713016a0944878cdc81958fe2647a4052e10e"}},"id":"prt_e3433b1d20017e6Exrvim6mGJW","sessionID":"ses_1cbccf440ffesSExN0HGL84oGD","messageID":"msg_e3433a2d1001y0KSRkYy3DEVNB"}}
