{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778992279534,"sessionID":"ses_1cbccf440ffesSExN0HGL84oGD","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_QxBIMfcfEtstTeFxFdXnGDEA","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r15s0\n+title: Exact source-read gating\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark mixes many immediate and single-source instructions with a smaller\n+  number of true register-register dependencies. The current load-use and\n+  forwarding compares still look at both source fields on every cycle, which\n+  adds always-on fanout and can create false stalls on instructions that do\n+  not architecturally read rs2.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add exact `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` bits to the fetch-time control bundle,\n+  derived from the same validated opcode/funct classification the decoder\n+  already uses, and route those bits into both the load-use interlock and the\n+  EX-stage forwarding compares. Keep ambiguous cases pessimistic so illegal or\n+  uncertain instructions still stall rather than risking an architectural miss.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Extend the control bundle with conservative uses_rs1 and uses_rs2 metadata.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Populate the source-read bits from the validated opcode/funct classification without changing legality rules.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Connect the new decoder outputs into the latched fetch-time control bundle.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the source-read metadata into the hazard and forwarding units.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use compares with the source-read bits so unused rs fields cannot trigger false stalls.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Prune unnecessary rs compare logic when the current instruction does not read a source register.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r15s0\n+title: Exact source-read gating\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark mixes many immediate and single-source instructions with a smaller\n+  number of true register-register dependencies. The current load-use and\n+  forwarding compares still look at both source fields on every cycle, which\n+  adds always-on fanout and can create false stalls on instructions that do\n+  not architecturally read rs2.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add exact `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` bits to the fetch-time control bundle,\n+  derived from the same validated opcode/funct classification the decoder\n+  already uses, and route those bits into both the load-use interlock and the\n+  EX-stage forwarding compares. Keep ambiguous cases pessimistic so illegal or\n+  uncertain instructions still stall rather than risking an architectural miss.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Extend the control bundle with conservative uses_rs1 and uses_rs2 metadata.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Populate the source-read bits from the validated opcode/funct classification without changing legality rules.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Connect the new decoder outputs into the latched fetch-time control bundle.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the source-read metadata into the hazard and forwarding units.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use compares with the source-read bits so unused rs fields cannot trigger false stalls.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Prune unnecessary rs compare logic when the current instruction does not read a source register.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r15s0\n+title: Exact source-read gating\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark mixes many immediate and single-source instructions with a smaller\n+  number of true register-register dependencies. The current load-use and\n+  forwarding compares still look at both source fields on every cycle, which\n+  adds always-on fanout and can create false stalls on instructions that do\n+  not architecturally read rs2.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add exact `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` bits to the fetch-time control bundle,\n+  derived 