{"type":"text","timestamp":1778990026235,"sessionID":"ses_1cbef47e5ffeJvI9bM4oYfB4Gw","part":{"id":"prt_e34118dda001mICohOhoTLXDvC","messageID":"msg_e34113c43001AA43WRoJvgkzMx","sessionID":"ses_1cbef47e5ffeJvI9bM4oYfB4Gw","type":"text","text":"I’ve settled on the decode-hoist angle: push the validated control bundle into fetch so ID stops rebuilding it on the hot path. I’m writing that as the hypothesis YAML now.","time":{"start":1778990026202,"end":1778990026229},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_086b47b59e481f5e016a093bc9f4808195b1f6fb36ac4b7a97","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778990027504,"sessionID":"ses_1cbef47e5ffeJvI9bM4oYfB4Gw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_QngDeB6Mw2QQP3IzfUBsWqBu","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r12s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260517-002-r12s1\n+title: \"Hoist full decode into fetch\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  ID still rebuilds the validated control bundle from the raw instruction on every cycle.\n+  Since fetch already owns the instruction slice, hoisting decode one stage earlier should\n+  shorten the hot IF/ID -> ID/EX path and reduce instruction fanout without changing\n+  retirement, trap, or RVFI behavior.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Extend the IF/ID bundle with a fully decoded control record, instantiate the existing\n+  decoder at fetch time, and latch that control alongside the predecoded instruction\n+  metadata. Then make ID a narrower register-read stage that consumes the latched control\n+  bundle instead of rebuilding opcode/funct legality and control signals locally. This keeps\n+  the ISA contract identical while removing the decoder case tree from the ID critical path.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Extend the IF/ID bundle with a latched control record so fetch can hand decode results forward with the instruction.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Decode each fetched instruction once at fetch time and carry the validated control bundle forward with the predecoded metadata.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consume the latched control bundle and remove the local decoder/control-tree work from the hot ID path.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r12s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r12s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r12s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r12s1.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@\n+id: hyp-20260517-002-r12s1\n+title: \"Hoist full decode into fetch\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  ID still rebuilds the validated control bundle from the raw instruction on every cycle.\n+  Since fetch already owns the instruction slice, hoisting decode one stage earlier should\n+  shorten the hot IF/ID -> ID/EX path and reduce instruction fanout without changing\n+  retirement, trap, or RVFI behavior.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Extend the IF/ID bundle with a fully decoded control record, instantiate the existing\n+  decoder at fetch time, and latch that control alongside the predecoded instruction\n+  metadata. Then make ID a narrower register-read stage that consumes the latched control\n+  bundle instead of rebuilding opcode/funct legality and control signals locally. This keeps\n+  the ISA contract identical while removing the decoder case tree from the ID critical path.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Extend the IF/ID bundle with a latched control record so fetch can hand decode results forward with the instruction.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Decode each fetched instruction once at fetch time and carry the validated control bundle forward with the predecoded metadata.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consume the latched control bundle and remove the local decoder/control-tree work from the hot ID path.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r12s1.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r12s1.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r12s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r12s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r12s1.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@\n+id: hyp-20260517-002-r12s1\n+title: \"Hoist full decode into fetch\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  ID still rebuilds the validated control bundle from the raw instruction on every cycle.\n+  Since fetch already owns the instruction slice, hoisting decode one stage earlier should\n+  shorten the hot IF/ID -> ID/EX path and reduce instruction fanout without changing\n+  retirement, trap, or RVFI behavior.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Extend the IF/ID bundle with a fully decoded control record, instantiate the existing\n+  decoder at fetch time, and latch that control alongside the predecoded instruction\n+  metadata. Then make ID a narrower register-read stage that consumes the latched control\n+  bundle instead of rebuilding opcode/funct legality and control signals locally. This keeps\n+  the ISA contract identical while removing the decoder case tree from the ID critical path.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Extend the IF/ID bundle with a latched control record so fetch can hand decode results forward with the instruction.\"\n+  