{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778990032247,"sessionID":"ses_1cbef47e5ffeJvI9bM4oYfB4Gw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_fn2gg8vp6j3qai76pMdiVmTi","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r12s1.yaml","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r12s1.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260517-002-r12s1\n2: title: \"Hoist full decode into fetch\"\n3: category: structural\n4: motivation: |\n5:   ID still rebuilds the validated control bundle from the raw instruction on every cycle.\n6:   Since fetch already owns the instruction slice, hoisting decode one stage earlier should\n7:   shorten the hot IF/ID -> ID/EX path and reduce instruction fanout without changing\n8:   retirement, trap, or RVFI behavior.\n9: hypothesis: |\n10:   Extend the IF/ID bundle with a fully decoded control record, instantiate the existing\n11:   decoder at fetch time, and latch that control alongside the predecoded instruction\n12:   metadata. Then make ID a narrower register-read stage that consumes the latched control\n13:   bundle instead of rebuilding opcode/funct legality and control signals locally. This keeps\n14:   the ISA contract identical while removing the decoder case tree from the ID critical path.\n15: expected_impact:\n16:   fitness_delta_pct: 4\n17:   confidence: medium\n18: changes:\n19:   - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n20:     description: \"Extend the IF/ID bundle with a latched control record so fetch can hand decode results forward with the instruction.\"\n21:   - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n22:     description: \"Decode each fetched instruction once at fetch time and carry the validated control bundle forward with the predecoded metadata.\"\n23:   - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n24:     description: \"Consume the latched control bundle and remove the local decoder/control-tree work from the hot ID path.\"\n\n(End of file - total 24 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260517-002-r12s1\ntitle: \"Hoist full decode into fetch\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  ID still rebuilds the validated control bundle from the raw instruction on every cycle.\n  Since fetch already owns the instruction slice, hoisting decode one stage earlier should\n  shorten the hot IF/ID -> ID/EX path and reduce instruction fanout without changing\n  retirement, trap, or RVFI behavior.\nhypothesis: |\n  Extend the IF/ID bundle with a fully decoded control record, instantiate the existing\n  decoder at fetch time, and latch that control alongside the predecoded instruction\n  metadata. Then make ID a narrower register-read stage that consumes the latched control\n  bundle instead of rebuilding opcode/funct legality and control signals locally. This keeps\n  the ISA contract identical while removing the decoder case tree from the ID critical path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Extend the IF/ID bundle with a latched control record so fetch can hand decode results forward with the instruction.\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r12s1.yaml","time":{"start":1778990032185,"end":1778990032243}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_093791d7d64ff315016a093bcfff70819791d5dc067cd5694a"}},"id":"prt_e3411a533001VPLfaSsZrGW5ba","sessionID":"ses_1cbef47e5ffeJvI9bM4oYfB4Gw","messageID":"msg_e341196a8001ebrIW4O5tlyAW4"}}
