\": \"Extend the ID/EX bundle with a latched pc_plus4 field.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and store pc_plus4 alongside the decoded instruction metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Reuse the latched pc_plus4 for JAL writeback and sequential next-PC selection.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the ID/EX bundle with a latched pc_plus4 field.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and store pc_plus4 alongside the decoded instruction metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Reuse the latched pc_plus4 for JAL writeback and sequential next-PC selection.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 311.83, ...\n  Line 9: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r3s1\", \"title\": \"Reuse ID target for JAL\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"EX still rebuilds the PC-relative jump target for JAL even though the\\nsame PC+imm value is already available from ID. Reusing that latched\\ntarget should trim another 32-bit adder from the execute-side timing\\npath without changing retirement, trap, or RVFI behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"EX still rebuilds the PC-relative jump target for JAL even though the\\nsame PC+imm value is already available from ID. Reusing that latched\\ntarget should trim another 32-bit adder from the execute-side timing\\npath without changing retirement, trap, or RVFI behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Use the precomputed ID-stage branch target for JAL redirects and\\nmisalignment checks, and leave EX to compute only the rs1+imm target\\nneeded for JALR. This keeps control flow identical while removing one\\nmore hot add/mux pair from the EX critical path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Reuse