   - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n27:     description: \"Drive the regfile from the narrow writeback bundle with no dependency on RVFI-only fields.\"\n28:   - file: rtl/core.sv\n29:     description: \"Wire RVFI from the separate retirement snapshot while keeping bypass and regfile traffic on the narrow path.\"\n\n(End of file - total 29 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260517-002-r13s1\ntitle: \"Split writeback from RVFI\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current post-MEM boundary still carries RVFI-only state through the same\n  bundle used by the regfile and bypass network. That makes the hottest retire\n  path wider than it needs to be on every instruction, even though the\n  forwarding logic only needs a narrow writeback view.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split the MEM/WB interface into a narrow writeback bundle and a separate\n  retirement snapshot. Keep rd/rd_wdata/valid/reg_write on the path used by\n  the regfile and forwarding network, and move RVFI-only fields onto a sideband\n  that is consumed only at the core boundary. This should reduce fanout and\n  routing pressure on the always-on post-MEM path without changing retirement\n  semantics.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r13s1.yaml","time":{"start":1778990735307,"end":1778990735326}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_04ff2f39c43d8218016a093e8f2dd881959e8abd19bca9a252"}},"id":"prt_e341c5fb0001C3F3WqIKVTgAch","sessionID":"ses_1cbe55ca0ffe5uO6odBkwh0T7L","messageID":"msg_e341c53110016kW8Isryw8e4di"}}
