edict statically. A predictor with no training state\\nshould be cheap enough for this tiny FPGA core.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Fold a purely combinational BTFNT hint into IF: predict backward\\nconditional branches taken, forward conditional branches not taken, and\\ndirect JALs taken. Keep EX redirect as the architectural source of truth\\nso mispredict recovery stays simple and RVFI/trap behavior is unchanged,\\nbut hide more fetch bubbles on CoreMark's hot loops.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a stateless static branch-direction predictor that chooses the speculative next PC while still yielding to EX-stage redirects.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a stateless static branch-direction predictor that chooses the speculative next PC while still yielding to EX-stage redirects.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: insn_beq_ch0\\nsummary: counterexample trace: insn_blt_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY  0:18:39 [insn_blt_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_insn_check_sv_178_115 at rvfi_insn_check.sv:178.7-178.76 step 20\\nSBY  0:18:39 [insn_blt_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\nSBY  0:22:11 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ...\n  Line 14: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r5s0\", \"title\": \"Remove regfile write-first bypass\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The regfile currently spends combinational logic on same-cycle write-first\\nbypassing for both read ports. That path is redundant with the existing\\nEX-stage forwarding network, and it sits on every decode-cycle operand read.\\nSimplifying it should trim a small but always-active hot path without\\nchanging architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The regfile currently spends combinational logic on same-cycle write-first\\nbypassing for both read ports. That path is redundant with the existing\\nEX-stage forwarding network, and it sits on every decode-cycle operand read.\\nSimplifying it should trim a small but always-active hot path without\\nchanging architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Remove the write-first bypass muxes from `reg_file.sv` and rely on the\\nexisting pipeline forwarding to supply younger values when an instruction\\nreaches EX. The ID stage still reads the register array combinationally, but\\nsame-cycle WB-to-ID visibility is no longer implemented inside the regfile,\\nwhich should reduce read-port fanout and improve Fmax.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/reg_file.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the same-cycle write-first read bypass so the read ports become simple array reads with only x0 special-casing.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/reg_file.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the same-cycle write-first read bypass so the read ports become simple array reads with only x0 special-casing.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 308.96, \"delta_pct\": -1.06, \"vs_baseline\": 9.24, \"fmax_mhz\": 138.77, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10266, \"ff\": 1898, \"seeds\": [132.36, 138.77, 143.35], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\"...\n  Line 15: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r5s1\", \"title\": \"Predecode instruction slices\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current decode path repeatedly fans the full 32-bit instruction into\\ndecoder, imm_gen, and hazard logic. A narrower predecode record should cut\\ncombinational fanout and bit-slicing depth in the hot IF/ID -> ID/EX path\\nwithout changing any architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current decode path repeatedly fans the full 32-bit instruction into\\ndecoder, imm_gen, and hazard logic. A narrower predecode record should cut\\ncombinational fanout and bit-slicing depth in the hot IF/ID -> ID/EX path\\nwithout changing any architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a compact predecode bundle in IF that latches opcode, funct3/funct7,\\nrd/rs1/rs2, and the already-formed immediate fragments, then have ID use\\nthose narrow fields instead of re-slicing the raw instruction everywhere.\\nThis is a structural timing cleanup aimed at reducing the decode-critical\\npath and top-level instruction fanout while keeping RVFI, traps, and\\nretirement order unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a compact predecode bundle to carry opcode/funct and register slices through IF/ID.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Capture the predecode bundle alongside the fetched instruction so downstream logic sees narrow fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the predecoded slices instead of repeatedly extracting them from the full instruction word.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor decode to operate on predecoded opcode/funct inputs while keeping legality checks unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/imm_gen.sv\", \"description\": \"Optionally source immediate fragments from the predecode bundle to shorten decode fanout.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl...\n  Line 17: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r6s0\", \"title\": \"Operand-use hazard gating\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The core already predecodes opcode and register slices, but the hazard\\nand forwarding logic still compares raw rs fields for