{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778991415207,"sessionID":"ses_1cbdaa750ffeEKojB10d0Fz4Y7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_MDKsFN4pRaxLGy2Jsg3Esokp","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"regfile|reg_file|write-first|bypass|x0 special-casing","path":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl","include":"*.jsonl"},"output":"Found 6 matches\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\n  Line 2: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Zero-wait load bypass\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark is load-heavy, and the current 5-stage pipe pays a full bubble\\non every load-use pair even when the data memory is zero-wait. Removing\\nthat unnecessary interlock should raise iterations per cycle without\\nchanging the ISA or the top-level RVFI contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark is load-heavy, and the current 5-stage pipe pays a full bubble\\non every load-use pair even when the data memory is zero-wait. Removing\\nthat unnecessary interlock should raise iterations per cycle without\\nchanging the ISA or the top-level RVFI contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a combinational MEM-to-EX bypass for load results so a dependent\\ninstruction can consume the loaded word in the next cycle instead of\\nstalling behind the load. Keep the existing dmem backpressure stall\\npath intact, but stop treating zero-wait load-use pairs as mandatory\\nbubbles.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the combinational load result and metadata needed for a same-cycle bypass.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a forwarding input that can source operands directly from the current MEM-stage load data.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Relax the load-use interlock when the zero-wait MEM bypass can satisfy the dependency.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the new MEM-stage bypass signals through the pipeline.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the combinational load result and metadata needed for a same-cycle bypass.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a forwarding input that can source operands directly from the current MEM-stage load data.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Relax the load-use inter...\n  Line 11: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r4s0\", \"title\": \"Latch writeback data in MEM\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"WB still rebuilds the final rd_wdata with a small mem_to_reg mux, and that\\nsignal fans out to both the regfile write port and the EX forwarding path.\\nHoisting the selection into MEM should shorten the common retire fanout\\nwithout changing architectural results.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"WB still rebuilds the final rd_wdata with a small mem_to_reg mux, and that\\nsignal fans out to both the regfile write port and the EX forwarding path.\\nHoisting the selection into MEM should shorten the common retire fanout\\nwithout changing architectural results.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a latched rd_wdata field to the MEM/WB bundle, compute it in\\nmem_stage.sv, and have wb_stage.sv forward that preselected value directly\\nto the regfile and bypass network. This keeps the ISA and RVFI behavior\\nunchanged while removing one more mux from the hot writeback path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the MEM/WB bundle with a latched rd_wdata field so writeback no longer has to remux ALU versus load data.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the final writeback value alongside the existing load-data path and store it in the MEM/WB register.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/wb_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the final mem_to_reg mux with a direct pass-through of the preselected writeback value.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the MEM/WB bundle with a latched rd_wdata field so writeback no longer has to remux ALU versus load data.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the final writeback value alongside the existing load-data path and store it in the MEM/WB register.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/wb_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the final mem_to_reg mux w...\n  Line 14: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r5s0\", \"title\": \"Remove regfile write-first bypass\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The regfile currently spends combinational logic on same-cycle write-first\\nbypassing for both read ports. That path is redundant with the existing\\nEX-stage forwarding network, and it sits on every decode-cycle operand read.\\nSimplifying it should trim a small but always-active hot path without\\nchanging architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The regfile currently spends combinational logic on same-cycle write-first\\nbypassing for both read ports. That path is redundant with the existing\\nEX-stage forwarding network, and it sits on every decode-cycle operand read.\\nSimplifying it should trim a small but always-active hot path without\\nchanging architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Remove the write-first bypass muxes from `reg_file.sv` and rely on the\\nexisting pipeline forwarding to supply younger values when an instruction\\nreaches EX. The ID stage still reads the register array combinationally, but\\nsame-cycle WB-to-ID visibility is no longer implemented inside the regfile,\\nwhich should reduce read-port fanout and improve Fmax.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/reg_file.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the same-cycle write-first read bypass so the read ports become simple array reads with only x0 special-casing.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/reg_file.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the same-cycle write-first read bypass so the read ports become simple array reads with only x0 special-casing.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 308.96, \"delta_pct\": -1.06, \"vs_baseline\": 9.24, \"fmax_mhz\": 138.77, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10266, \"ff\": 1898, \"seeds\": [132.36, 138.77, 143.35], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\"...\n  Line 30: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r10s1\", \"title\": \"Split retire and writeback\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current MEM/WB boundary carries a lot of RVFI-only state through the\\nsame bundle that feeds the regfile and forwarding logic. That makes the\\nhottest post-MEM path wider than it needs to be.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current MEM/WB boundary carries a lot of RVFI-only state through the\\nsame bundle that feeds the regfile and forwarding logic. That makes the\\nhottest post-MEM path wider than it needs to be.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split the wide retirement snapshot from the narrow writeback/bypass path:\\nkeep only rd, rd_wdata, reg_write, and valid on the signals used by the\\nregfile and forwarding network, and carry the full RVFI snapshot on a\\nseparate sideband bundle. This should reduce fanout and routing pressure on\\nthe MEM/WB boundary without changing architectural retirement behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define separate narrow writeback and full retire-snapshot bundle types so the post-MEM path can be split cleanly.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the narrow writeback data separately from the full RVFI retirement snapshot.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the narrow writeback metadata instead of the full MEM/WB bundle for bypass comparisons.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/wb_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drive the regfile from the narrow writeback bundle with no dependency on RVFI-only fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the split bundles so RVFI comes from the retire snapshot while writeback and forwarding use the narrow path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define separate narrow writeback and full retire-snapshot bundle types so the post-MEM path can be split cleanly.\"}, {\"file\": \"r...\n  Line 39: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-002-r13s1\", \"title\": \"Split writeback from RVFI\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current post-MEM boundary still carries RVFI-only state through the same\\nbundle used by the regfile and bypass network. That makes the hottest retire\\npath wider than it needs to be on every instruction, even though the\\nforwarding logic only needs a narrow writeback view.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current post-MEM boundary still carries RVFI-only state through the same\\nbundle used by the regfile and bypass network. That makes the hottest retire\\npath wider than it needs to be on every instruction, even though the\\nforwarding logic only needs a narrow writeback view.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split the MEM/WB interface into a narrow writeback bundle and a separate\\nretirement snapshot. Keep rd/rd_wdata/valid/reg_write on the path used by\\nthe regfile and forwarding network, and move RVFI-only fields onto a sideband\\nthat is consumed only at the core boundary. This should reduce fanout and\\nrouting pressure on the always-on post-MEM path without changing retirement\\nsemantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define a narrow writeback bundle plus a separate retire snapshot so post-MEM state can be split cleanly.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the narrow writeback data independently from the RVFI snapshot at the MEM/WB boundary.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare against the narrow writeback metadata instead of the full retirement snapshot.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/wb_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drive the regfile from the narrow writeback bundle with no dependency on RVFI-only fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire RVFI from the separate retirement snapshot while keeping bypass and regfile traffic on the narrow path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\"...\n  Line 40: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-003-r13s2\", \"title\": \"Advisory BTFNT in fetch\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Fetch now already carries decoded control metadata, so a purely advisory\\nbackward-taken/forward-not-taken hint can be evaluated without adding a\\nseparate training structure. That gives CoreMark's hot loop backedges a\\nchance to bypass the EX-stage bubble while keeping the redirect contract\\nunchanged.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Fetch now already carries decoded control metadata, so a purely advisory\\nbackward-taken/forward-not-taken hint can be evaluated without adding a\\nseparate training structure. That gives CoreMark's hot loop backedges a\\nchance to bypass the EX-stage bubble while keeping the redirect contract\\nunchanged.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a stateless BTFNT next-PC hint inside `rtl/if_stage.sv` that\\nspeculatively chooses the decoded branch target for backward conditional\\nbranches and direct JALs, while falling through on forward branches and\\nleaving JALR/EX redirects untouched. Because fetch already owns decode\\nmetadata, this should recover some loop bubbles without introducing\\npredictor state, update logic, or RVFI-visible behavior changes.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a stateless BTFNT-style speculative next-PC hint in fetch, but keep EX-stage redirect authoritative and avoid any predictor update state.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a stateless BTFNT-style speculative next-PC hint in fetch, but keep EX-stage redirect authoritative and avoid any predictor update state.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: insn_beq_ch0\\nmmary: counterexample trace: insn_bltu_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY  1:13:47 [insn_bltu_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flat...","metadata":{"matches":6,"truncated":false},"title":"regfile|reg_file|write-first|bypass|x0 special-casing","time":{"start":1778991415196,"end":1778991415206}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0f29bfbbe89d1241016a094136fe748193b8a9d11eeb49d006"}},"id":"prt_e3426bf9a001wEkGjPZ7cEIFhk","sessionID":"ses_1cbdaa750ffeEKojB10d0Fz4Y7","messageID":"msg_e3426b212002wF3L0uB8ioxviJ"}}
