 \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current decode path repeatedly fans the full 32-bit instruction into\\ndecoder, imm_gen, and hazard logic. A narrower predecode record should cut\\ncombinational fanout and bit-slicing depth in the hot IF/ID -> ID/EX path\\nwithout changing any architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current decode path repeatedly fans the full 32-bit instruction into\\ndecoder, imm_gen, and hazard logic. A narrower predecode record should cut\\ncombinational fanout and bit-slicing depth in the hot IF/ID -> ID/EX path\\nwithout changing any architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a compact predecode bundle in IF that latches opcode, funct3/funct7,\\nrd/rs1/rs2, and the already-formed immediate fragments, then have ID use\\nthose narrow fields instead of re-slicing the raw instruction everywhere.\\nThis is a structural timing cleanup aimed at reducing the decode-critical\\npath and top-level instruction fanout while keeping RVFI, traps, and\\nretirement order unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a compact predecode bundle to carry opcode/funct and register slices through IF/ID.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Capture the predecode bundle alongside the fetched instruction so downstream logic sees narrow fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the predecoded slices instead of repeatedly extracting them from the full instruction word.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor decode to operate on predecoded opcode/funct inputs while keeping legality checks unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/imm_gen.sv\", \"description\": \"Optionally source immediate fragments from the predecode bundle to shorten decode fanout.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file