ption\": \"Use predictor output to select the speculative next PC before EX resolution, but keep EX redirects as the ...\n  Line 17: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r6s0\", \"title\": \"Operand-use hazard gating\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The core already predecodes opcode and register slices, but the hazard\\nand forwarding logic still compares raw rs fields for every instruction.\\nThat creates avoidable compare fanout and can also stall on rs2 bits that\\nare really immediates in single-source instructions.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The core already predecodes opcode and register slices, but the hazard\\nand forwarding logic still compares raw rs fields for every instruction.\\nThat creates avoidable compare fanout and can also stall on rs2 bits that\\nare really immediates in single-source instructions.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add predecoded operand-use flags so the pipe only compares rs1/rs2 when\\nthe current instruction actually reads them. Carry those flags through\\nIF/ID and ID/EX, then gate load-use detection and EX forwarding selects\\nwith them to remove spurious stalls and trim hot compare logic without\\nchanging RVFI or retirement behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the pipeline bundles with operand-use bits for rs1/rs2 so downstream hazard and forwarding logic can ignore unused source fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Predecode which source operands are actually read and carry those bits alongside the fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the operand-use flags into ID/EX so execute-side forwarding can skip irrelevant source compares.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use checks with the operand-use flags to avoid false stalls on immediate and single-source instructions.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the operand-use flags to prune unnecessary rs compare logic in the EX-stage forwarding network.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"c...\n  Line 18: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r6s1\", \"title\": \"(slot 1 hypothesis-gen failed)\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"hypothesis_gen_failed: Hypothesis agent modified off-limits paths and was rolled back: ['cores/bench/rtl/core.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv']\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 6, \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark is heavy on loads and stores, and `mem_stage.sv` still recomputes\\nbyte masks, address alignment, and load shift behavior from `alu_result`\\nand `mem_width` on every memory op. Moving that address-derived metadata\\nearlier should shorten the hot memory path and reduce fanout without\\nchanging any architectural results.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add precomputed memory-lane metadata to the EX/MEM bundle: word-aligned\\naddress, byte mask, shift amount, and misalignment status. Have\\n`ex_stage.sv` derive those fields once from `alu_result[1:0]` and\\n`mem_width`, then let `mem_stage.sv` consume them directly so it only\\ngates the bus and forms the final load value. This is a structural\\ncleanup aimed at trimming the memory-access critical path while keeping\\nRVFI, traps, and retirement order unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the EX/MEM bundle with precomputed memory-lane metadata such as aligned address, byte mask, shift amount, and misalign flag.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive the memory-lane metadata once from the ALU result and load/store width before the MEM stage.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the precomputed lane metadata so the memory stage no longer repeats width-based mask, alignment, and shift logic.\"}]}, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-002-r6s1 (broken, n/a): Structural hot-path cleanup onl...\n  Line 19: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r6s2\", \"title\": \"Advisory loop-backedge predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends cycles on repeated loop backedges and direct jumps,\\nso the core keeps paying the EX-stage fetch bubble on control transfers\\nthat are cheap to predict statically. A predictor with no training state\\nis the lowest-risk way to hide more of that control-flow latency.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends cycles on repeated loop backedges and direct jumps,\\nso the core keeps paying the EX-stage fetch bubble on control transfers\\nthat are cheap to predict statically. A predictor with no training state\\nis the lowest-risk way to hide more of that control-flow latency.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a purely combinational BTFNT-style hint in IF: predict direct JALs\\ntaken and predict conditional branches taken only when the immediate is\\nbackward, while forward branches fall through. Keep EX-stage resolution\\nas the architectural source of truth for redirects and mispredict repair,\\nso the predictor only changes speculative fetch and not RVFI behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a stateless static branch-direction hint in fetch, but leave EX redirects and wrong-path squashing authoritative.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a stateless static branch-direction hint in fetch, but leave EX redirects and wrong-p