o much in IF logic, state,\\nor formal complexity. A very small predictor that only tracks the most\\nrecent conditional backedge should be cheaper than a BTB or return stack\\nwhile still removing a common fetch bubble.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends a lot of time on the same loop backedges, but the\\nbroader predictor attempts so far have paid too much in IF logic, state,\\nor formal complexity. A very small predictor that only tracks the most\\nrecent conditional backedge should be cheaper than a BTB or return stack\\nwhile still removing a common fetch bubble.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny one-entry loop-backedge predictor in IF that remembers the last\\ntaken conditional branch PC, its target, and a single taken bit. Speculate\\nonly on exact PC hits for backward conditional branches, update only from\\nretired conditional branches, and keep EX-stage redirect authoritative for\\nrecovery. This narrows the predictor enough to avoid the fanout and control\\ncomplexity that hurt earlier predictor ideas while still targeting CoreMark's\\ndominant loop pattern.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the loop-backedge hint to choose the speculative next PC on exact-hit backward branches, but always yield to EX-stage redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire retired conditional-branch outcome information into the predictor update path without changing the RVFI or trap contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a single-entry loop-backedge predictor with one-bit taken state, exact PC tagging, and conservative fall-through on miss.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"conf...\n  Line 32: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r11s0\", \"title\": \"Cache pc+4 in IF\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The sequential fall-through PC is needed on every instruction, but the\\ncurrent core still recomputes `pc + 4` in ID. Hoisting that universal add\\ninto fetch should trim a small amount of always-on decode-path logic and\\nreduce fanout through the hot IF/ID -> ID/EX boundary.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The sequential fall-through PC is needed on every instruction, but the\\ncurrent core still recomputes `pc + 4` in ID. Hoisting that universal add\\ninto fetch should trim a small amount of always-on decode-path logic and\\nreduce fanout through the hot IF/ID -> ID/EX boundary.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a cached `pc_plus4` field to the IF/ID bundle, compute it once in\\n`if_stage.sv`, and have `id_stage.sv` latch that value directly instead of\\nrebuilding `pc + 4` every cycle. This keeps retirement, traps, and RVFI\\nbehavior unchanged while moving a universal 32-bit add out of the ID hot\\npath.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add `pc_plus4` to the IF/ID bundle so fetch can carry the sequential PC forward.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch `pc_plus4` alongside the fetched instruction metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the cached sequential PC instead of recomputing `pc + 4` in decode.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add `pc_plus4` to the IF/ID bundle so fetch can carry the sequential PC forward.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch `pc_plus4` alongside the fetched instruction metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the cached sequential PC instead of recomputing `pc + 4` in decode.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 310.99, \"delta_pct\": -9.25, \"vs_baseline\": 9.9...\n  Line 33: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260