his should prune irrelevant compare logic\\nfor instructions that do not read a source register while keeping all\\nambiguous cases pessimistic so RVFI, traps, and retirement order stay the\\nsame.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the control/predecode bundles with conservative `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Populate the source-read metadata from the validated opcode/funct classification without changing legality rules.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the source-read metadata with the fetched instruction so downstream logic can use it without re-decoding.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate the load-use compare tree with the source-read metadata so unused source fields cannot trigger false stalls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/for...\n  Line 42: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-002-r14s1\", \"title\": \"Replicate regfile read banks\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The ID stage hits the register file on every instruction, and the shared\\nread-side structure still fans the same storage and bypass compare logic into\\nboth operand ports. Duplicating the read path should shorten that always-on\\noperand cone and give Fmax headroom without changing architectural state.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The ID stage hits the register file on every instruction, and the shared\\nread-side structure still fans the same storage and bypass compare logic into\\nboth operand ports. Duplicating the read path should shorten that always-on\\noperand cone and give Fmax headroom without changing architectural state.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Rework `reg_file.sv` into two read-port-private copies of the 32x32 register\\narray, with one broadcast write port keeping both copies coherent and the\\nexisting same-cycle write-first behavior preserved per port. This is a\\nstructural timing play: each read port gets a smaller, more local mux tree,\\nreducing fanout on the hottest decode-to-execute operand path while leaving\\nvisible register semantics unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/reg_file.sv\", \"description\": \"Split the register storage into two read-port-specific copies and keep x0, write-first bypass, and write coherence behavior identical.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/reg_file.sv\", \"description\": \"Split the register storage into two read-port-specific copies and keep x0, write-first bypass, and write coherence behavior identical.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 275.17, \"delta_pct\": -21.26, \"vs_baseline\": -2.7, \"fmax_mhz\": 123.59, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9781, \"ff\": 1963, \"seeds\": [118.01, 137.48, 123.59], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"e...\n  Line 43: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-003-r14s2\", \"title\": \"Retired loop-backedge predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark keeps revisiting the same short loop backedges, so the core still\\npays the EX-stage branch bubble on a very regular control-flow pattern.\\nA tiny predictor anchored to retired branch state should recover some of\\nthat lost fetch bandwidth without introducing broad BTB or return-stack\\nmachinery.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark keeps revisiting the same short loop backedges, so the core still\\npays the EX-stage branch bubble on a very regular control-flow pattern.\\nA tiny predictor anchored to retired branch state should recover some of\\nthat lost fetch bandwidth without introducing broad BTB or return-stack\\nmachinery.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a single-entry retired loop-backedge predictor that caches the last\\ntaken backward conditional branch PC, its target, and a small confidence\\ncounter. Speculate only on exact-PC hits for that loop, train only from\\nretired branch outcomes, and keep EX-stage redirect authoritative for\\nrecovery so fetch never owns architectural control flow.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the predictor's speculative next PC on exact-hit backward branches, but always yield to EX-stage redirects.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire retired branch PC, target, and taken outcome into the predictor update path without changing RVFI behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a one-entry loop-backedge predictor with exact-PC tagging, a cached target, and conservative fall-through on miss.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the predictor's speculative next PC on exact-hit backward branches, but always yield to EX-stage redirects.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire retired...","metadata":{"matches":42,"truncated":false},"title":"hyp-20260517-002-r15s1|structural|forward_unit|id_stage|if_stage|mem_stage|retire|rvfi|bundle","time":{"start":1778992225748,"end":1778992225772}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_05bd09a157153f0b016a09446185148195979a3781e4728e5c"}},"id":"prt_e34331d4f0019GQHu77r35JiB2","sessionID":"ses_1cbccf4f2ffedkJmz451hcfyaA","messageID":"msg_e34330ba6001VM5VQ07sL7hD2N"}}
