{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778992288191,"sessionID":"ses_1cbccf4f2ffedkJmz451hcfyaA","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_qC0LJXjbOWGxc1S8YhBM9Ht8","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r15s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260517-002-r15s1\n+title: \"Retime forwarding into ID\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The execute stage still carries the operand muxing cone on every ALU,\n+  branch, and JALR path. On this core, that makes EX responsible for both\n+  selecting the right source value and doing the actual work, which is a\n+  poor fit for FPGA timing.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Move the forwarding selection for rs1/rs2 up into `id_stage.sv` so the\n+  ID/EX register latches already-selected operand values, then let\n+  `ex_stage.sv` consume those latched operands directly. Keep the existing\n+  forwarding comparisons and producer priority rules intact, but retime the\n+  muxes out of EX to shrink the critical execute cone without changing\n+  retirement behavior.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add or adjust ID/EX bundle fields if needed so the latched operands can carry the selected rs1/rs2 values cleanly.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Rewire the forwarding outputs into ID and pass the preselected operand values into EX instead of muxing there.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Apply forwarding to the read operands before they are latched into ID/EX.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Drop the operand-selection muxes and consume the already-forwarded operands directly.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r15s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/c