nch target before EX resolves the branch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire retired conditional-branch outcome information into the predictor update path without changing the RVFI or trap contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny direct-mapped 2-bit branch-direction table with conservative fall-through defaults and retirement-time updates.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use a small bimodal direction predictor to speculatively choose fall-through vs...","metadata":{"matches":1,"truncated":false},"title":"hyp-20260516-003-r9s2","time":{"start":1778990642237,"end":1778990642243}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0acc7b020a5a5b75016a093e321bc48197ba0687101fa53ecf"}},"id":"prt_e341af43c001uzVY8REmqw0s7w","sessionID":"ses_1cbe55b85ffeSfXCysNCLpVqZc","messageID":"msg_e341ac6d20010J3tEd9C8D7nn6"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778990642271,"sessionID":"ses_1cbe55b85ffeSfXCysNCLpVqZc","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_kmbtBHndnK20toQZrTp3FMBS","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"hyp-20260517-002-r12s1","path":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl","include":"log.jsonl"},"output":"Found 1 matches\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\n  Line 36: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-002-r12s1\", \"title\": \"Hoist full decode into fetch\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"ID still rebuilds the validated control bundle from the raw instruction on every cycle.\\nSince fetch already owns the instruction slice, hoisting decode one stage earlier should\\nshorten the hot IF/ID -> ID/EX path and reduce instruction fanout without changing\\nretirement, trap, or RVFI behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"ID still rebuilds the validated control bundle from the raw instruction on every cycle.\\nSince fetch already owns the instruction slice, hoisting decode one stage earlier should\\nshorten the hot IF/ID -> ID/EX path and reduce instruction fanout without changing\\nretirement, trap, or RVFI behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Extend the IF/ID bundle with a fully decoded control record, instantiate the existing\\ndecoder at fetch time, and latch that control alongside the predecoded instruction\\nmetadata. Then make ID a narrower register-read stage that consumes the latched control\\nbundle instead of rebuilding opcode/funct legality and control signals locally. This keeps\\nthe ISA contract identical while removing the decoder case tree from the ID critical path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the IF/ID bundle with a latched control record so fetch can hand decode results forward with the instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode each fetched instruction once at fetch time and carry the validated control bundle forward with the predecoded metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the latched control bundle and remove the local decoder/control-tree work from the hot ID path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the IF/ID bundle with a latched control record so fetch can hand decode results fo...","metadata":{"matches":1,"truncated":false},"title":"hyp-20260517-002-r12s1","time":{"start":1778990642265,"end":1778990642271}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0acc7b020a5a5b75016a093e321bd88197aac9aa51a88d35e7"}},"id":"prt_e341af458001UCtYSDmtq8qnMS","sessionID":"ses_1cbe55b85ffeSfXCysNCLpVqZc","messageID":"msg_e341ac6d20010J3tEd9C8D7nn6"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778990642272,"sessionID":"ses_1cbe55b85ffeSfXCysNCLpVqZc","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_EGkCKX7AeeSk8vOWeFvmhyJJ","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"hyp-20260516-003-r10s2","path":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl","include":"log.jsonl"},"output":"Found 1 matches\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\n  Line 31: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r10s2\", \"title\": \"Narrow loop-backedge predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends a lot of time on the same loop backedges, but the\\nbroader predictor attempts so far have paid too much in IF logic, state,\\nor formal complexity. A very small predictor that only tracks the most\\nrecent conditional backedge should be cheaper than a BTB or return stack\\nwhile still removing a common fetch bubble.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends a lot of time on the same loop backedges, but the\\nbroader predictor attempts so far have paid too much in IF logic, state,\\nor formal complexity. A very small predictor that only tracks the most\\nrecent conditional backedge should be cheaper than a BTB or return stack\\nwhile still removing a common fetch bubble.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny one-entry loop-backedge predictor in IF that remembers the last\\ntaken conditional branch PC, its target, and a single taken bit. Speculate\\nonly on exact PC hits for backward conditional branches, update only from\\nretired conditional branches, and keep EX-stage redirect authoritative for\\nrecovery. This narrows the predictor enough to avoid the fanout and control\\ncomplexity that hurt earlier predictor ideas while still targeting CoreMark's\\ndominant loop pattern.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the loop-backedge hint to choose the speculative next PC on exact-hit backward branches, but always yield to EX-stage redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire retired conditional-branch outcome information into the predictor update path without changing the RVFI or trap contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a single-entry loop-backedge predictor with one-bit taken state, exact PC tagging, and conservative fall-through on miss.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"conf...","metadata":{"matches":1,"truncated":false},"title":"hyp-20260516-003-r10s2","time":{"start":1778990642263,"end":1778990642272}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0acc7b020a5a5b75016a093e321bd08197b27fa8540dd81ca0"}},"id":"prt_e341af44c001QEI7GGlBC7yG3f","sessionID":"ses_1cbe55b85ffeSfXCysNCLpVqZc","messageID":"msg_e341ac6d20010J3tEd9C8D7nn6"}}
