{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778991382555,"sessionID":"ses_1cbdaa7d0ffeJE5fARu2WqbUzQ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_tiVFzHMoGoJ1uNEEHMCUZr4I","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-003-r14s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260517-003-r14s2\n+title: \"Retired loop-backedge predictor\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark keeps revisiting the same short loop backedges, so the core still\n+  pays the EX-stage branch bubble on a very regular control-flow pattern.\n+  A tiny predictor anchored to retired branch state should recover some of\n+  that lost fetch bandwidth without introducing broad BTB or return-stack\n+  machinery.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a single-entry retired loop-backedge predictor that caches the last\n+  taken backward conditional branch PC, its target, and a small confidence\n+  counter. Speculate only on exact-PC hits for that loop, train only from\n+  retired branch outcomes, and keep EX-stage redirect authoritative for\n+  recovery so fetch never owns architectural control flow.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Use the predictor's speculative next PC on exact-hit backward branches, but always yield to EX-stage redirects.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire retired branch PC, target, and taken outcome into the predictor update path without changing RVFI behavior.\"\n+  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n+    description: \"Add a one-entry loop-backedge predictor with exact-PC tagging, a cached target, and conservative fall-through on miss.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-003-r14s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-2026051