: \"Tiny bimodal branch predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends a meaningful fraction of its time on the same\\nconditional backedges and short control-flow loops. The earlier static\\nand stack-based predictor ideas were either too expensive or too broad,\\nso a smaller learned direction predictor is the best remaining angle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends a meaningful fraction of its time on the same\\nconditional backedges and short control-flow loops. The earlier static\\nand stack-based predictor ideas were either too expensive or too broad,\\nso a smaller learned direction predictor is the best remaining angle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny direct-mapped bimodal predictor that stores only 2-bit taken\\nconfidence for conditional branches, with the existing IF-stage immediate\\ndecode used to choose between fall-through and the predicted branch target.\\nUpdate the table only from retired conditional branches, keep EX-stage\\nresolution authoritative for recovery, and avoid BTB or return-stack\\ntarget storage entirely so the predictor stays cheap enough for this FPGA.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use a small bimodal direction predictor to speculatively choose fall-through vs the decoded branch target before EX resolves the branch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire retired conditional-branch outcome information into the predictor update path without changing the RVFI or trap contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny direct-mapped 2-bit branch-direction table with conservative fall-through defaults and retirement-time updates.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use a small bimodal direction pre