{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778992230882,"sessionID":"ses_1cbccf5c3ffeCuSivYpjLU6M6C","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_7eCuEAYdvGHXG3RDyw1YwsQj","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-003-r12s2\"|\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-003-r14s2\"|\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r11s2\"","path":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl","include":"*.jsonl"},"output":"Found 3 matches\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\n  Line 34: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r11s2\", \"title\": \"Retired loop-backedge predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark still burns cycles on the same hot loop backedges, but the\\nbroader predictor attempts paid too much in IF logic or speculative\\nstate. A tiny predictor anchored to retired control-flow state is the\\nnarrowest remaining way to hide those fetch bubbles without changing\\nthe architectural redirect contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark still burns cycles on the same hot loop backedges, but the\\nbroader predictor attempts paid too much in IF logic or speculative\\nstate. A tiny predictor anchored to retired control-flow state is the\\nnarrowest remaining way to hide those fetch bubbles without changing\\nthe architectural redirect contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a single-entry loop-backedge predictor that remembers the most\\nrecent retired taken conditional branch PC and target, then speculates\\nonly on exact PC hits for backward branches. Train it strictly from\\nretired branch outcomes, keep EX-stage redirect authoritative for every\\nrecovery path, and avoid any extra speculative training state so the\\npredictor stays small enough to help CoreMark without dragging Fmax.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/