y to hide\\nfetch bubbles without changing the architectural redirect contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a single-entry loop-count predictor that remembers the most recent\\nretired backward conditional branch PC, its target, and a small trip-count\\nconfidence counter. Speculate only on exact-PC hits for that loop, train\\nonly from retired branch outcomes, and always let EX-stage redirect remain\\nthe source of truth for recovery so the predictor stays narrow and\\nCoreMark-focused.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the loop predictor to choose the speculative next PC for exact-hit backward branches while preserving EX-stage redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire retired branch PC, target, and taken/not-taken outcome into the predictor update path without changing RVFI behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a one-entry loop-count predictor with exact-PC tagging, cached target, and conservative fall-through on miss.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\"... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-001-r13s0\", \"title\": \"Source-read compare gating\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock still compares both source fields on every instruction,\\neven when the opcode never reads rs2. That burns always-on compare fanout and\\ncan inject false bubbles on common immediate-style CoreMark instructions.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock still compares both source fields on every instruction,\\neven when the opcode never reads rs2. That burns always-on compare fanout and\\ncan inject false bubbles on common immediate-style CoreMark instructions.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add exact `uses_rs1` and `uses_rs2` masks to the fetch-time predecode bundle,\\nderive them from the already-validated opcode class, and use them to gate the\\nload-use compare tree in `hazard_unit.sv`. Keep illegal or ambiguous cases\\npessimistic so the interlock only disappears when a source operand is definitely\\nunused.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the predecode bundle with exact source-read masks for rs1 and rs2.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch the source-read masks alongside the existing fetch-time predecode.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the new predecode masks into the hazard unit inputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate the load-use compare tree with the source-read masks so unused source fields cannot trigger false stalls.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the predecode bundle with exact source-read masks for rs1 and rs2.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch the source-read masks alongside the existing fetch-time predecode.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the new predecode masks into the hazard unit inputs.\"}, {\"file\":... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-002-r13s1\", \"title\": \"Split writeback from RVFI\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current post-MEM boundary still carries RVFI-only state through the same\\nbundle used by the regfile and bypass network. That makes the hottest retire\\npath wider than it needs to be on every instruction, even though the\\nforwarding logic only needs a narrow writeback view.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current post-MEM boundary still carries RVFI-only state through the same\\nbundle used by the regfile and bypass network. That makes the hottest retire\\npath wider than it needs to be on every instruction, even though the\\nforwarding logic only needs a narrow writeback view.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split the MEM/WB interface into a narrow writeback bundle and a separate\\nretirement snapshot. Keep rd/rd_wdata/valid/reg_write on the path used by\\nthe regfile and forwarding network, and move RVFI-only fields onto a sideband\\nthat is consumed only at the core boundary. This should reduce fanout and\\nrouting pressure on the always-on post-MEM path without changing retirement\\nsemantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define a narrow writeback bundle plus a separate retire snapshot so post-MEM state can be split cleanly.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the narrow writeback data independently from the RVFI snapshot at the MEM/WB boundary.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare against the narrow writeback metadata instead of the full retirement snapshot.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/wb_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drive the regfile from the narrow writeback bundle with no dependency on RVFI-only fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire RVFI from the separate retirement snapshot while keeping bypass and regfile traffic on the narrow path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\"... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-003-r13s2\", \"title\": \"Advisory BTFNT in fetch\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Fetch now already carries decoded control metadata, so a purely advisory\\nbackward-taken/forward-not-taken hint can be evaluated without adding a\\nseparate training structure. That gives CoreMark's hot loop backedges a\\nchance to bypass the EX-stage bubble while keeping the redirect contract\\nunchanged.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Fetch now already carries decoded control metadata, so a purely advisory\\nbackward-taken/forward-not-taken hint can be evaluated without adding a\\nseparate training structure. That gives CoreMark's hot loop backedges a\\nchance to bypass the EX-stage bubble while keeping the redirect contract\\nunchanged.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a stateless BTFNT next-PC hint inside `rtl/if_stage.sv` that\\nspeculatively chooses the decoded branch target for backward conditional\\nbranches and direct JALs, while falling through on forward branches and\\nleaving JALR/EX redirects untouched. Because fetch already owns decode\\nmetadata, this should recover some loop bubbles without introducing\\npredictor state, update logic, or RVFI-visible behavior changes.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a stateless BTFNT-style speculative next-PC hint in fetch, but keep EX-stage redirect authoritative and avoid any predictor update state.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a stateless BTFNT-style speculative next-PC hint in fetch, but keep EX-stage redirect authoritative and avoid any predictor update state.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: insn_beq_ch0\\nmmary: counterexample trace: insn_bltu_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY  1:13:47 [insn_bltu_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flat... (line truncated to 2000 chars)","truncated":true,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl","time":{"start":1778992230862,"end":1778992230888}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_067022dc2396366d016a094466c3848190b1faeffd0751ac19"}},"id":"prt_e343331ba001Hm7cMqWFirLNdO","sessionID":"ses_1cbccf5c3f